1802
02:21:36,460 --> 02:21:41,020
Disruption to shipping through the Strait of Hormuz is reshaping regional energy routes,

1803
02:21:41,020 --> 02:21:46,620
with Pakistan emerging as an alternative corridor. But higher costs, tighter fuel availability,

1804
02:21:46,620 --> 02:21:50,940
and peak summer demand are placing an increasing strain on energy systems.

1805
02:21:50,940 --> 02:21:53,660
Osama bin Javed reports from Karachi Port.

1806
02:21:55,090 --> 02:21:59,890
There's a rush to reach Karachi Port. The facility has handled more traffic in a month

1807
02:21:59,890 --> 02:22:03,650
than the whole of last year. That's because Pakistan, as Iran's neighbour,

1808
02:22:03,650 --> 02:22:07,810
offers some of the first safe seaports as ships exit the Strait of Hormuz.

1809
02:22:08,370 --> 02:22:11,890
The crisis comes as Pakistan's preparing for peak summer demand.

1810
02:22:11,890 --> 02:22:15,970
It's headed towards a deepening energy crunch across both the power sector

1811
02:22:15,970 --> 02:22:21,230
and fuel supply chain. The biggest challenge is liquefied natural gas or LNG,

1812
02:22:21,230 --> 02:22:24,350
which accounts for more than 21% of electricity generation.

1813
02:22:24,990 --> 02:22:27,950
Officials say supplies could fall to near zero from April.

1814
02:22:28,860 --> 02:22:33,340
At the same time, the global energy shock is feeding directly into domestic costs.

1815
02:22:33,420 --> 02:22:37,900
Pakistan is operating with just 24 days of gasoline and diesel stocks.

1816
02:22:37,900 --> 02:22:41,980
War risk insurance premiums for tankers have surged more than 10-fold.

1817
02:22:42,540 --> 02:22:46,380
Fate rates have quadrupled. To manage volatility,

1818
02:22:46,380 --> 02:22:49,340
the government has moved to weekly fuel price adjustments.

1819
02:22:49,340 --> 02:22:54,540
Industry analysts describe March as the moment Pakistan's energy system was stress test.

1820
02:22:54,540 --> 02:22:58,460
It's more severe external shock since the 1970s oil crisis.

1821
02:22:58,460 --> 02:23:02,060
Pakistan moved quickly on multiple fronts simultaneously.

1822
02:23:02,060 --> 02:23:06,780
Diplomatically, it secured rerouted cargoes through the Red Sea port of Janpo.

1823
02:23:06,780 --> 02:23:10,620
Naval escorts kept tankers moving through contested corridors.

1824
02:23:10,620 --> 02:23:14,700
Pakistani flag tankers have also passed the Strait with permission from Iran.

1825
02:23:14,700 --> 02:23:19,980
It was a very coherent institutional response that operated faster than most observers expected.

1826
02:23:20,780 --> 02:23:24,460
Now, a hybrid strategy is in the making to keep the lights on.

1827
02:23:24,460 --> 02:23:28,540
It includes limited daily load shedding, compulsory conservation measures,

1828
02:23:28,540 --> 02:23:30,300
and higher electricity tariffs.

1829
02:23:30,860 --> 02:23:34,220
The government is offering a $7 a month targeted relief

1830
02:23:34,220 --> 02:23:39,420
for motorcyclists and wickshaw drivers, even as it increases petroleum levees to manage

1831
02:23:39,420 --> 02:23:45,780
fiscal pressure. Oil tankers like these provide the nearly 80% of energy that Pakistan requires

1832
02:23:45,780 --> 02:23:48,020
