1962
02:31:59,150 --> 02:32:02,430
and the rulings of the International Court of Justice

1963
02:32:02,430 --> 02:32:05,390
that this is an illegal occupation that must end.

1964
02:32:06,640 --> 02:32:08,640
For hundreds of thousands of Palestinians

1965
02:32:08,640 --> 02:32:11,200
made homeless by Israel's war on Gaza,

1966
02:32:11,200 --> 02:32:13,120
every day is a struggle.

1967
02:32:13,120 --> 02:32:16,080
As bombed out neighborhoods are slowly cleared of rubble,

1968
02:32:16,080 --> 02:32:19,600
some families are collecting scrap metal to survive.

1969
02:32:19,600 --> 02:32:21,920
Ali Mahmoud reports from Gaza City.

1970
02:32:25,710 --> 02:32:28,270
Trucks arrive one after another,

1971
02:32:28,270 --> 02:32:31,950
offloading what remains of homes, shops and entire streets.

1972
02:32:33,100 --> 02:32:35,020
Across large part of Gaza,

1973
02:32:35,020 --> 02:32:38,380
rubble removal continues month after Israeli bombardment

1974
02:32:38,380 --> 02:32:39,820
flat an entire neighborhood.

1975
02:32:40,740 --> 02:32:43,060
But for some, these dumping grounds

1976
02:32:43,060 --> 02:32:45,060
are more than just fields of debris.

1977
02:32:46,100 --> 02:32:47,380
They are workplaces.

1978
02:32:48,260 --> 02:32:51,140
Children search the mountains of broken concrete

1979
02:32:51,140 --> 02:32:53,780
and twisted metal for anything they can sell.

1980
02:32:54,500 --> 02:32:56,740
Wood, copper wire, aluminum.

1981
02:32:58,530 --> 02:33:01,250
Each piece they collect means a few more coins.

1982
02:33:02,320 --> 02:33:06,480
Each truck brings another opportunity and another risk.

1983
02:33:07,650 --> 02:33:09,570
The ground is unstable.

1984
02:33:09,570 --> 02:33:11,730
Sharp edges just from broken walls.

1985
02:33:12,290 --> 02:33:13,490
Aid agents is worn.

1986
02:33:13,490 --> 02:33:17,250
Unexploded ordinance may still be buried beneath the debris.

1987
02:33:18,700 --> 02:33:22,700
Isan Abdelal lives in a tent near one of the dumping sites.

1988
02:33:23,260 --> 02:33:30,780
We come here hoping to earn 20 shakals, about six dollars.

1989
02:33:30,780 --> 02:33:32,060
But it comes at a cost.

1990
02:33:32,700 --> 02:33:35,580
Injuries, exhaustion, cuts everywhere.

1991
02:33:35,580 --> 02:33:37,180
You can see the wounds and the blood.

1992
02:33:38,610 --> 02:33:41,170
The war has left hundreds of thousands of families

1993
02:33:41,170 --> 02:33:42,450
without stable income.

1994
02:33:43,570 --> 02:33:46,210
Factories are shut, shops are gone.

1995
02:33:46,210 --> 02:33:48,290
Entire businesses reduced to dust.

1996
02:33:49,520 --> 02:33:53,360
Post-war recovery is measured by reconstruction in plans,

1997
02:33:53,360 --> 02:33:54,560
funding in pledges.

1998
02:33:54,560 --> 02:33:57,360
But here on the ground recovery looks different.

1999
02:33:57,360 --> 02:34:00,480
It looks like children navigating the rubble,

2000
02:34:00,480 --> 02:34:03,600
households depending on the fragments of what was destroyed.

2001
02:34:03,600 --> 02:34:07,120
As long as livelihood remains absent

2002
02:34:07,120 --> 02:34:09,120
and reconstruction uncertain,

2003
02:34:09,120 --> 02:34:11,840
the rubble will continue to serve two purposes.

2004
02:34:12,640 --> 02:34:15,200
One reminder of loss.

2005
02:34:15,200 --> 02:34:18,480
And for some people it is a means of survival.

2006
02:34:19,570 --> 02:34:23,490
Informal scrap collection has become one of the few ways to earn cash.

2007
02:34:26,450 --> 02:34:28,770
We come here to earn money for food.

2008
02:34:28,770 --> 02:34:31,170
My father has no work, so we have to come.

2009
02:34:33,730 --> 02:34:38,690
We come here hoping to find bits of wood or pieces of cable that we can sell.

2010
02:34:38,690 --> 02:34:41,410
Anything that may help us buy food for our children.

2011
02:34:41,410 --> 02:34:44,690
We know climbing onto the moving trucks is dangerous.

2012
02:34:44,690 --> 02:34:47,330
But when your family depends on it, you take the risk.

2013
02:34:48,290 --> 02:34:52,180
Parents say they don't want their children here.

2014
02:34:52,180 --> 02:34:55,140
But survival leaves little room for a choice.

2015
02:34:56,370 --> 02:35:00,770
And Mahmoud Al-Jazeera from Gaza City, Palestine.

2016
02:35:01,700 --> 02:35:04,660
Serbia says explosives have been found near a pipeline

2017
02:35:04,660 --> 02:35:07,220
that carries Russian gas to Hungary.

2018
02:35:07,220 --> 02:35:12,180
Authorities say the discovery was made outside a Serbian town near the Hungarian border.

2019
02:35:12,180 --> 02:35:16,020
It comes just a week before closely watched elections in Hungary.

2020
02:35:16,100 --> 02:35:20,660
Prime Minister Viktor Orban is fighting to extend his 16 years in power.

2021
02:35:20,660 --> 02:35:23,220
He's linked Ukraine to those explosives.

2022
02:35:26,450 --> 02:35:31,010
For years, Ukraine has been working to cut Europe off from Russian energy.

2023
02:35:31,010 --> 02:35:32,770
They blew up Nord Stream.

2024
02:35:32,770 --> 02:35:35,330
Shut down the gas pipelines supplying Hungary.

2025
02:35:35,330 --> 02:35:40,210
And this year placed Hungary under an oil blockade by closing the Družba pipeline.

2026
02:35:40,210 --> 02:35:44,130
The Russian section of the Turk Stream is also under continuous military attack.

2027
02:35:44,210 --> 02:35:47,730
Ukraine's efforts pose a life-threatening danger to Hungary.

2028
02:35:48,580 --> 02:35:50,820
Kyiv has rejected Orban's accusations.

2029
02:35:50,820 --> 02:35:53,620
Posting on X, the foreign ministry spokesman said,

2030
02:35:53,620 --> 02:35:55,860
Ukraine has nothing to do with this.

2031
02:35:55,860 --> 02:35:59,300
Most probably it's a Russian false flag operation

2032
02:35:59,300 --> 02:36:03,460
as part of Moscow's heavy interference in Hungarian elections.

2033
02:36:04,540 --> 02:36:08,220
It's been a subdued Easter in the occupied Palestinian territories

2034
02:36:08,220 --> 02:36:11,980
where ceremonies have been scaled back because of the Iran war.

2035
02:36:11,980 --> 02:36:17,100
A small Sunday Mass was held at the Church of the Holy Sepulcher in occupied East Jerusalem.

2036
02:36:17,100 --> 02:36:20,300
The site is revered by Christians as the traditional site

2037
02:36:20,300 --> 02:36:23,820
of Jesus Christ's crucifixion and resurrection.

2038
02:36:23,820 --> 02:36:26,460
Israeli authorities have limited access.

2039
02:36:26,460 --> 02:36:28,220
On Palm Sunday last week,

2040
02:36:28,220 --> 02:36:31,340
a Latin patriarch was blocked from entering the Church,

2041
02:36:31,340 --> 02:36:33,500
sparking international condemnation.

2042
02:36:39,360 --> 02:36:43,360
In Gaza, Orthodox Palestinian Christians who follow the Eastern calendar

2043
02:36:43,360 --> 02:36:45,280
have celebrated Palm Sunday.

2044
02:36:45,280 --> 02:36:50,110
It marks the beginning of the Holy Week leading to Orthodox Easter.

2045
02:36:50,110 --> 02:36:54,270
Worshippers attended Mass at the St. Porphyrios Church in Gaza City.

2046
02:36:54,270 --> 02:36:57,950
It came under Israeli attack several times before the ceasefire.

2047
02:36:58,990 --> 02:37:01,630
White scrups are warning about threats to media freedom

2048
02:37:01,630 --> 02:37:05,790
in Sahel countries that have seen military coups in recent years.

2049
02:37:05,790 --> 02:37:11,390
Junta leaders are using security concerns and cybercrime laws to silence criticism.

2050
02:37:11,390 --> 02:37:14,670
Reporters Without Borders has condemned the sentencing last week

2051
02:37:14,670 --> 02:37:18,270
of a Malian journalist convicted of insulting the military leader

2052
02:37:18,270 --> 02:37:20,670
of Niger, Imogen Kimber, reports.

2053
02:37:22,370 --> 02:37:24,130
Words can be life-changing.

2054
02:37:24,130 --> 02:37:26,210
They certainly were for Yusuf Sissoko,

2055
02:37:26,850 --> 02:37:31,250
the publishing director of the Malian newspaper L'Alternance or The Alternating.

2056
02:37:31,810 --> 02:37:35,250
This article accuses General Abdur Rahman Tieny,

2057
02:37:35,250 --> 02:37:37,250
the military leader of neighboring Niger,

2058
02:37:37,250 --> 02:37:40,290
of trying to distract people from his government's security failures.

2059
02:37:40,690 --> 02:37:45,740
Tieny had blamed the attacks on the international airport

2060
02:37:45,740 --> 02:37:49,180
in the capital Niami back in January on France,

2061
02:37:49,180 --> 02:37:52,620
the Ivory Coast and Benin without providing evidence.

2062
02:37:52,620 --> 02:37:54,620
The Islamic State claimed responsibility.

2063
02:37:56,080 --> 02:38:00,160
The article argues Tieny overlooked the threat posed by armed groups,

2064
02:38:00,160 --> 02:38:03,600
which he pledged to remove when he seized power in 2023.

2065
02:38:04,370 --> 02:38:09,410
It also accuses what he calls Tieny's military regime of economic suicide,

2066
02:38:09,490 --> 02:38:11,410
citing the closure of borders with Benin.

2067
02:38:13,390 --> 02:38:17,310
Niger is a landlocked country which relied on its neighbor's ports for trade.

2068
02:38:18,340 --> 02:38:21,940
Sissoko was convicted last week of spreading false news,

2069
02:38:21,940 --> 02:38:26,100
undermining the credibility of the state and insulting a foreign head of state.

2070
02:38:26,660 --> 02:38:30,900
He was fined $1,700 and sentenced to two years in prison.

2071
02:38:32,500 --> 02:38:35,860
This journalist would only speak anonymously for fear of reprisals.

2072
02:38:35,860 --> 02:38:40,580
It represents a setback for freedom of expression,

2073
02:38:40,580 --> 02:38:42,980
which is already under severe strain in Mali,

2074
02:38:42,980 --> 02:38:46,180
but we do not use hope that there is still the possibility of appeal.

2075
02:38:47,920 --> 02:38:52,560
Rather than the press law, Sissoko was charged under Mali's cybercrime law,

2076
02:38:52,560 --> 02:38:56,320
which allows journalists to be punished for criticizing not just their own state,

2077
02:38:56,320 --> 02:38:57,440
but others in the Sahel.

2078
02:39:00,560 --> 02:39:02,720
Which makes the situation even more complex.

2079
02:39:02,720 --> 02:39:05,200
Had it been handled as a press-related matter,

2080
02:39:05,200 --> 02:39:07,360
the sentence might not have been the same.

2081
02:39:07,360 --> 02:39:10,480
I see this ruling as a strong message to all media actors,

2082
02:39:10,480 --> 02:39:13,440
that things can go very far, so extreme caution is needed.

2083
02:39:14,960 --> 02:39:17,120
And this isn't just happening in Mali.

2084
02:39:17,120 --> 02:39:19,040
In Niger and Burkina Faso,

2085
02:39:19,040 --> 02:39:22,400
military-led governments are restricting freedom of expression

2086
02:39:22,400 --> 02:39:24,960
by suspending independent media outlets

2087
02:39:24,960 --> 02:39:27,440
and censoring and intimidating reporters.

2088
02:39:27,440 --> 02:39:30,480
They're also targeting social media activists and influencers.

2089
02:39:31,120 --> 02:39:34,400
In Burkina Faso, some journalists who criticize the military

2090
02:39:34,400 --> 02:39:38,400
have been forcibly conscripted without training to fight against armed groups.

2091
02:39:39,330 --> 02:39:42,050
With the widening crackdown on independent journalism,

2092
02:39:42,050 --> 02:39:46,450
the International Press Institute is warning of an information blackout in the Sahel,

2093
02:39:47,010 --> 02:39:50,370
which it says could have regional and global consequences.

2094
02:39:51,170 --> 02:39:52,850
Imogen Kimber, Al Jazeera.

2095
02:40:00,000 --> 02:40:03,320
a city with a huge gun violence problem.

2096
02:40:03,320 --> 02:40:06,280
It's just renewed a deal for a system of sensors

2097
02:40:06,280 --> 02:40:10,280
that detects gunshots and then sends drones to crime scenes.

2098
02:40:10,280 --> 02:40:12,720
But critics say they target black communities

2099
02:40:12,720 --> 02:40:16,920
and make little difference, as Phil LaValle reports.

2100
02:40:16,920 --> 02:40:18,680
I see anything like that.

2101
02:40:18,680 --> 02:40:21,160
Cherie and Rosalyn are two mums

2102
02:40:21,160 --> 02:40:24,520
with the most painful bond imaginable.

2103
02:40:24,520 --> 02:40:29,520
Imagine seeing your loved one shot over 12 or 13 times.

2104
02:40:31,140 --> 02:40:34,740
That picture would never go out my head.

2105
02:40:34,740 --> 02:40:37,500
Both received a heart-breaking call.

2106
02:40:37,500 --> 02:40:39,900
Their sons had been shot dead.

2107
02:40:39,900 --> 02:40:44,870
Different men, but same day, one year apart.

2108
02:40:44,870 --> 02:40:47,150
I remember that day like yesterday.

2109
02:40:47,150 --> 02:40:48,830
I remember pulling up on the scene

2110
02:40:48,830 --> 02:40:55,140
and seeing the vehicle shot up, blood on the car.

2111
02:40:56,100 --> 02:40:57,900
There are hundreds of stories like this

2112
02:40:57,900 --> 02:41:02,060
here in Birmingham, Alabama, all with the same ending.

2113
02:41:02,060 --> 02:41:04,140
Gun violence is rife.

2114
02:41:04,140 --> 02:41:07,300
Could AI have saved any of them?

2115
02:41:07,300 --> 02:41:09,540
It doesn't work, no.

2116
02:41:09,540 --> 02:41:11,380
And that is what this is all about

2117
02:41:11,380 --> 02:41:13,260
because AI is being used here

2118
02:41:13,260 --> 02:41:15,340
to try to combat gun violence.

2119
02:41:15,340 --> 02:41:18,020
There is this network of sensors dotted around

2120
02:41:18,020 --> 02:41:19,860
listening for the sound of gunshots.

2121
02:41:19,860 --> 02:41:22,380
They hear them and they dispatch police automatically,

2122
02:41:22,380 --> 02:41:24,660
but where those sensors are located,

2123
02:41:24,660 --> 02:41:26,060
that's what's controversial.

2124
02:41:26,060 --> 02:41:30,260
These devices are placed in predominantly poor neighborhoods.

2125
02:41:30,260 --> 02:41:32,060
They're placed in black and brown neighborhoods.

2126
02:41:32,060 --> 02:41:34,700
And what it means is more police presence.

2127
02:41:34,700 --> 02:41:35,700
Multiple sensors.

2128
02:41:35,700 --> 02:41:37,540
The technology has been used in cities

2129
02:41:37,540 --> 02:41:39,500
across the US for years,

2130
02:41:39,500 --> 02:41:43,260
yet many are rolling it back or cancelling it altogether.

2131
02:41:43,260 --> 02:41:46,500
But in this city, synonymous with the civil rights movement,

2132
02:41:46,500 --> 02:41:48,340
they have just spent millions of dollars

2133
02:41:48,340 --> 02:41:49,860
to extend the contract.

2134
02:41:49,860 --> 02:41:51,580
On top of that, they've added drones

2135
02:41:51,580 --> 02:41:53,180
which take off autonomously

2136
02:41:53,180 --> 02:41:55,300
and can get to the scene of any potential crime

2137
02:41:55,300 --> 02:41:56,820
long before the police can.

2138
02:41:56,820 --> 02:42:00,900
Birmingham saw a 44% drop in homicides last year.

2139
02:42:00,900 --> 02:42:02,700
That is a 10-year low.

2140
02:42:02,700 --> 02:42:07,220
Another statistic, 88% of victims were black.

2141
02:42:07,220 --> 02:42:09,700
It's evident that it's not working.

2142
02:42:09,700 --> 02:42:13,460
It's not the technology that's keeping us safe.

2143
02:42:13,460 --> 02:42:15,340
And it may be other reasons

2144
02:42:15,340 --> 02:42:17,820
why crime is not as prevalent.

2145
02:42:17,820 --> 02:42:20,490
The company behind the tech says

2146
02:42:20,490 --> 02:42:24,570
it has seen a reduction of 61% in gunfire incidents

2147
02:42:24,570 --> 02:42:26,250
over the last two years

2148
02:42:26,250 --> 02:42:29,930
and that it helps because up to 85% of gunshots

2149
02:42:29,930 --> 02:42:32,170
are never reported by residents.

2150
02:42:32,170 --> 02:42:36,130
There are some areas where we do respond to shootings,

2151
02:42:36,130 --> 02:42:37,810
but we don't get a 911 call.

2152
02:42:37,810 --> 02:42:39,930
We identify those areas as a priority.

2153
02:42:39,930 --> 02:42:41,770
And it is solely the police

2154
02:42:41,770 --> 02:42:44,930
who choose which neighborhoods to put sensors in.

2155
02:42:44,930 --> 02:42:48,770
The family members that won't forget, that's retaliation.

2156
02:42:48,770 --> 02:42:50,370
That's what worries these bums.

2157
02:42:50,370 --> 02:42:53,450
Shootings lead to revenge and more shootings.

2158
02:42:53,450 --> 02:42:56,570
They spend their lives now consoling other parents

2159
02:42:56,570 --> 02:42:59,010
and trying to break that cycle.

2160
02:42:59,010 --> 02:43:02,660
I'll never be healed until I make it up there.

2161
02:43:02,660 --> 02:43:04,300
That's my goal.

2162
02:43:04,300 --> 02:43:06,380
I'm gonna make it up there with him.

2163
02:43:06,380 --> 02:43:08,300
For these mums, it is not about the sounds

2164
02:43:08,300 --> 02:43:11,420
that are picked up, but the silence that follows

2165
02:43:11,420 --> 02:43:14,220
and the emptiness it leaves behind.

2166
02:43:14,220 --> 02:43:18,460
Phil Lavelle, Al Jazeera, Birmingham, Alabama.

2167
02:43:18,460 --> 02:43:20,140
My name's gonna be here in a couple of minutes

2168
02:43:20,140 --> 02:43:23,340
with more coverage of the Israel-U.S. and Iran war.

2169
02:43:23,340 --> 02:43:24,340
I'm Rob Matheson.

2170
02:43:24,340 --> 02:43:26,180
Stay with us on Al Jazeera.

2171
02:43:27,790 --> 02:43:29,950
The latest news as it breaks.

2172
02:43:29,950 --> 02:43:32,950
What this front from Yemen is going to represent to Israel

2173
02:43:32,950 --> 02:43:36,430
is a threat from air and a threat from sea.

2174
02:43:36,430 --> 02:43:37,830
With live coverage.

2175
02:43:37,830 --> 02:43:39,030
A clear message from Iran.

2176
