4531
05:33:38,370 --> 05:33:40,050
Across large part of Gaza,

4532
05:33:40,250 --> 05:33:43,570
rubble removal continues month after its raided bombardment

4533
05:33:43,570 --> 05:33:45,290
in a flat and entire neighborhood.

4534
05:33:46,050 --> 05:33:50,330
But for some, these dumping grounds are more than just fields of debris.

4535
05:33:51,340 --> 05:33:52,660
They are workplaces.

4536
05:33:53,450 --> 05:33:56,330
Children search the mountains of broken concrete

4537
05:33:56,330 --> 05:33:59,010
and a twisted metal for anything they can sell.

4538
05:33:59,650 --> 05:34:01,970
Wood, copper wire, aluminum.

4539
05:34:03,790 --> 05:34:06,590
Each piece they collect means a few more coins.

4540
05:34:07,580 --> 05:34:11,780
Each truck brings another opportunity and another risk.

4541
05:34:12,910 --> 05:34:14,350
The ground is unstable.

4542
05:34:14,750 --> 05:34:17,070
Sharp edges from broken walls.

4543
05:34:17,510 --> 05:34:20,190
Aid agents is worn, unexploded ordnance

4544
05:34:20,190 --> 05:34:22,470
may still be buried beneath the debris.

4545
05:34:23,960 --> 05:34:27,880
Hussana Abdel-A'al lives in a tent near one of the dumping sites.

4546
05:34:32,000 --> 05:34:35,720
We come here hoping to earn 20 shekels, about six dollars.

4547
05:34:36,040 --> 05:34:37,400
But it comes at a cost.

4548
05:34:37,840 --> 05:34:40,360
Injuries, exhaustion, cuts everywhere.

4549
05:34:40,760 --> 05:34:42,400
You can see the wounds and the blood.

4550
05:34:43,280 --> 05:34:46,350
The war has left hundreds of thousands of families

4551
05:34:46,350 --> 05:34:47,710
without stable income.

4552
05:34:48,660 --> 05:34:51,180
Factories are shut, shops are gone.

4553
05:34:51,380 --> 05:34:53,540
Entire businesses reduced to dust.

4554
05:34:54,660 --> 05:34:58,460
Post-war recovery is measured by reconstruction in plans,

4555
05:34:58,460 --> 05:34:59,500
funding in pledges.

4556
05:34:59,740 --> 05:35:02,300
But here on the ground, recovery looks different.

4557
05:35:02,500 --> 05:35:05,500
It looks like children navigating the rubble,

4558
05:35:05,500 --> 05:35:08,460
households depending on the fragments of what was destroyed.

4559
05:35:08,780 --> 05:35:11,980
As long as livelihood remains absent

4560
05:35:12,340 --> 05:35:14,140
and reconstruction uncertain,

4561
05:35:14,300 --> 05:35:17,140
the rubble will continue to serve two purposes.

4562
05:35:17,780 --> 05:35:20,060
One reminder of loss.

4563
05:35:20,460 --> 05:35:23,700
And for some people, it is a means of survival.

4564
05:35:24,780 --> 05:35:28,900
Informal scrap collection has become one of the few ways to earn cash.

4565
05:35:31,660 --> 05:35:33,780
We come here to earn money for food.

4566
05:35:33,940 --> 05:35:36,500
My father has no work, so we have to come.

4567
05:35:36,660 --> 05:35:43,460
We come here hoping to find bits of wood or pieces of cable that we can sell.

4568
05:35:43,660 --> 05:35:46,220
Anything that may help us buy food for our children.

4569
05:35:46,500 --> 05:35:49,500
We know climbing onto the moving trucks is dangerous.

4570
05:35:49,780 --> 05:35:52,420
But when your family depends on it, you take the risk.

4571
05:35:55,050 --> 05:35:57,650
Parents say they don't want their children here.

4572
05:35:58,050 --> 05:36:01,010
But survival leaves little room for a choice.

4573
05:36:02,150 --> 05:36:06,590
An Mahmoud Al-Jazeera from Gaza City, Palestine.

4574
05:36:08,180 --> 05:36:11,620
Serbia says explosives have been found near a pipeline

4575
05:36:11,620 --> 05:36:13,820
that carries Russian gas to Hungary.

4576
05:36:14,260 --> 05:36:19,100
Though it is say the discovery was made outside a Serbian town near the Hungarian border.

4577
05:36:19,620 --> 05:36:23,380
It comes just a week before closely watched elections in Hungary.

4578
05:36:23,500 --> 05:36:28,060
Prime Minister Viktor Orban is fighting to extend his 16 years in power.

4579
05:36:28,620 --> 05:36:30,900
He's linked Ukraine to those explosives.

4580
05:36:31,750 --> 05:36:34,070
Orkiva's rejected Orban's accusations,

4581
05:36:34,070 --> 05:36:36,950
posting on X, the foreign ministry spokesman said,

4582
05:36:37,390 --> 05:36:39,230
Ukraine has nothing to do with this.

4583
05:36:39,230 --> 05:36:43,590
Most probably a Russian false flag operation as part of Moscow's heavy

4584
05:36:43,590 --> 05:36:46,430
interference in Hungarian elections.

4585
05:36:48,570 --> 05:36:52,090
It's been a subdued Easter in the occupied Palestinian territories

4586
05:36:52,090 --> 05:36:55,650
where ceremonies have been scaled back because of the Iran war.

4587
05:36:56,290 --> 05:37:02,770
A small Sunday mass was held at the church of the Holy Sepulchre in occupied East Jerusalem.

4588
05:37:03,610 --> 05:37:07,690
The site is revered by Christians as the traditional site

4589
05:37:07,690 --> 05:37:11,450
of Jesus Christ's crucification and resurrection.

4590
05:37:11,610 --> 05:37:20,570
Israeli authorities have limited access in Gaza.

4591
05:37:20,570 --> 05:37:24,090
Orthodox Palestinian Christians who follow the Eastern calendar

4592
05:37:24,090 --> 05:37:26,370
have celebrated Palm Sunday.

4593
05:37:26,370 --> 05:37:30,370
It marks the beginning of the Holy Week leading to Orthodox Easter.

4594
05:37:30,850 --> 05:37:36,010
Worshipers attended mass at the Saint Peripherous Church in Gaza City.

4595
05:37:36,900 --> 05:37:40,220
It came under Israeli attacks several times before the ceasefire.

4596
05:37:42,340 --> 05:37:46,860
Rights groups are warning about threats to media freedom in Sahel countries

4597
05:37:46,860 --> 05:37:48,940
that have seen military coups in recent years.

4598
05:37:48,940 --> 05:37:54,100
Junta leaders are using security concerns and cybercrime laws to silence criticism.

4599
05:37:54,780 --> 05:37:57,980
Reporters without borders has condemned the sentencing last week

4600
05:37:57,980 --> 05:38:03,220
of a Malian journalist convicted of insulting the military leader of Niger.

4601
05:38:03,580 --> 05:38:07,910
Midden Kimber reports, words can be life changing.

4602
05:38:08,390 --> 05:38:11,070
They certainly were for Yusuf Cisoko,

4603
05:38:11,110 --> 05:38:15,470
the publishing director of the Malian newspaper, L'Alternance, or The Alternating.

4604
05:38:16,030 --> 05:38:19,230
This article accuses General Abdul Rahman Tieny,

4605
05:38:19,470 --> 05:38:21,470
the military leader of neighboring Niger,

4606
05:38:21,470 --> 05:38:24,550
of trying to distract people from his government's security failures.

4607
05:38:26,770 --> 05:38:29,930
Tieny had blamed the attacks on the international airport

4608
05:38:29,930 --> 05:38:33,450
in the capital Niyami back in January on France,

4609
05:38:33,450 --> 05:38:36,450
the Ivory Coast and Benin without providing evidence.

4610
05:38:37,740 --> 05:38:39,700
The Islamic State claimed responsibility.

4611
05:38:41,170 --> 05:38:45,250
The article argues Tieny overlooked the threat posed by armed groups,

4612
05:38:45,250 --> 05:38:48,690
which he pledged to remove when he seized power in 2023.

4613
05:38:49,420 --> 05:38:54,220
It also accuses what he calls Tieny's military regime of economic suicide,

4614
05:38:54,460 --> 05:38:56,460
citing the closure of borders with Benin.

4615
05:38:58,730 --> 05:39:02,770
Niger is a landlocked country which relied on its neighbor's ports for trade.

4616
05:39:03,630 --> 05:39:07,110
Cisoko was convicted last week of spreading false news,

4617
05:39:07,110 --> 05:39:11,510
undermining the credibility of the state and insulting a foreign head of state.

4618
05:39:12,070 --> 05:39:16,350
He was fined $1,700 and sentenced to two years in prison.

4619
05:39:17,890 --> 05:39:21,370
This journalist would only speak anonymously for fear of reprisals.

4620
05:39:23,570 --> 05:39:26,010
It represents a setback for freedom of expression,

4621
05:39:26,010 --> 05:39:28,450
which is already under severe strain in Mali,

4622
05:39:28,450 --> 05:39:31,690
but we do not use hope that there is still the possibility of appeal.

4623
05:39:33,340 --> 05:39:34,860
Rather than the press law,

4624
05:39:34,860 --> 05:39:38,060
Cisoko was charged under Mali's cybercrime law,

4625
05:39:38,060 --> 05:39:41,860
which allows journalists to be punished for criticising not just their own state,

4626
05:39:41,860 --> 05:39:43,020
but others in the Sahel.

4627
05:39:46,020 --> 05:39:48,180
Which makes the situation even more complex.

4628
05:39:48,180 --> 05:39:50,660
Had it been handled as a press-related matter,

4629
05:39:50,660 --> 05:39:52,780
the sentence might not have been the same.

4630
05:39:52,780 --> 05:39:55,940
I see this ruling as a strong message to all media actors,

4631
05:39:55,940 --> 05:39:58,940
that things can go very far, so extreme caution is needed.

4632
05:40:00,050 --> 05:40:02,050
And this isn't just happening in Mali.

4633
05:40:02,050 --> 05:40:04,050
In Niger and Burkina Faso,

4634
05:40:04,050 --> 05:40:07,050
military-led governments are restricting freedom of expression

4635
05:40:07,050 --> 05:40:10,050
by suspending independent media outlets

4636
05:40:10,050 --> 05:40:12,050
and censoring and intimidating reporters.

4637
05:40:12,050 --> 05:40:16,050
They're also targeting social media activists and influencers.

4638
05:40:16,050 --> 05:40:19,050
In Burkina Faso, some journalists who criticise the military

4639
05:40:19,050 --> 05:40:22,050
have been forcibly conscripted without training

4640
05:40:22,050 --> 05:40:24,050
to fight against armed groups.

4641
05:40:24,050 --> 05:40:27,140
With the widening crackdown on independent journalism,

4642
05:40:27,140 --> 05:40:29,140
the International Press Institute

4643
05:40:29,140 --> 05:40:32,140
is warning of an information blackout in the Sahel,

4644
05:40:32,140 --> 05:40:36,140
which it says could have regional and global consequences.

4645
05:40:36,140 --> 05:40:38,140
Imogen Kimber, Alger Zira.

4646
05:40:38,140 --> 05:40:42,850
How much can AI be used to stop gun deaths?

4647
05:40:42,850 --> 05:40:46,850
That's the question being asked in Birmingham, Alabama,

4648
05:40:46,850 --> 05:40:49,850
a city with a huge gun violence problem.

4649
05:40:49,850 --> 05:40:52,850
It's just renewed a deal for a system of sensors

4650
05:40:52,850 --> 05:40:56,850
that detects gunshots and then sends drones to crime scenes

4651
05:40:56,850 --> 05:40:58,850
to live out.

4652
05:40:58,850 --> 05:41:00,850
We'll see anything like that.

4653
05:41:00,850 --> 05:41:02,850
Cherie and Rosalyn are two mums

4654
05:41:02,850 --> 05:41:05,850
with the most painful bond imaginable.

4655
05:41:05,850 --> 05:41:11,850
Imagine seeing your loved one shot over 12 or 13 times.

4656
05:41:11,850 --> 05:41:15,870
That picture would never go out my head.

4657
05:41:15,870 --> 05:41:18,870
Both received a heartbreaking call.

4658
05:41:18,870 --> 05:41:21,870
Their sons had been shot dead.

4659
05:41:21,870 --> 05:41:25,870
Different men, but same day, one year apart.

4660
05:41:25,870 --> 05:41:27,870
I remember that day like yesterday.

4661
05:41:27,870 --> 05:41:31,870
I remember pulling up on the scene and seeing the vehicle

4662
05:41:31,870 --> 05:41:37,220
shot up, blood on the car.

4663
05:41:37,220 --> 05:41:39,220
There are hundreds of stories like this

4664
05:41:39,220 --> 05:41:41,220
here in Birmingham, Alabama,

4665
05:41:41,220 --> 05:41:43,220
all with the same ending.

4666
05:41:43,220 --> 05:41:45,220
Gun violence is rife.

4667
05:41:45,220 --> 05:41:48,220
Could AI have saved any of them?

4668
05:41:48,220 --> 05:41:50,220
It doesn't work.

4669
05:41:50,220 --> 05:41:52,220
And that is what this is all about

4670
05:41:52,220 --> 05:41:54,220
because AI is being used here

4671
05:41:54,220 --> 05:41:56,220
to try to combat gun violence.

4672
05:41:56,220 --> 05:41:59,220
There is this network of sensors dotted around

4673
05:41:59,220 --> 05:42:01,220
listening for the sound of gunshots.

4674
05:42:01,220 --> 05:42:03,220
They hear them and they dispatch police automatically,

4675
05:42:03,220 --> 05:42:05,220
but where those sensors are located,

4676
05:42:05,220 --> 05:42:07,220
that's what's controversial.

4677
05:42:07,220 --> 05:42:11,220
These devices are placed in predominantly poor neighborhoods.

4678
05:42:11,220 --> 05:42:13,220
They're placed in black and brown neighborhoods

4679
05:42:13,220 --> 05:42:16,220
and what it means is more police presence.

4680
05:42:16,220 --> 05:42:20,220
The technology has been used in cities across the US

4681
05:42:20,220 --> 05:42:22,220
for years, yet many are rolling it back

4682
05:42:22,220 --> 05:42:24,220
or cancelling it altogether.

4683
05:42:24,220 --> 05:42:27,220
But in this city, synonymous with the Civil Rights movement,

4684
05:42:27,220 --> 05:42:29,220
they have just spent millions of dollars

4685
05:42:29,220 --> 05:42:31,220
to extend the contract.

4686
05:42:31,220 --> 05:42:33,220
On top of that, they've added drones

4687
05:42:33,220 --> 05:42:35,220
which take off autonomously and can get to the scene

4688
05:42:35,220 --> 05:42:38,220
of any potential crime long before the police can.

4689
05:42:38,220 --> 05:42:42,220
Birmingham saw a 44% drop in homicides last year.

4690
05:42:42,220 --> 05:42:44,220
That is a 10-year low.

4691
05:42:44,220 --> 05:42:48,220
Another statistic, 88% of victims were black.

4692
05:42:48,220 --> 05:42:51,220
It's evident that it's not working.

4693
05:42:51,220 --> 05:42:54,220
It's not the technology that's keeping us safe

4694
05:42:54,220 --> 05:42:59,220
and it may be other reasons why crime is not as prevalent.

4695
05:42:59,220 --> 05:43:02,220
The company behind the tech says it has seen a reduction

4696
05:43:02,220 --> 05:43:06,220
of 61% in gunfire incidents over the last two years

4697
05:43:06,220 --> 05:43:10,220
and that it helps because up to 85% of gunshots

4698
05:43:10,220 --> 05:43:12,220
are never reported by residents.

4699
05:43:12,220 --> 05:43:16,220
There are some areas where we do respond to shootings

4700
05:43:16,220 --> 05:43:18,220
but we don't get a 911 call.

4701
05:43:18,220 --> 05:43:20,220
We identify those areas as a priority.

4702
05:43:20,220 --> 05:43:23,220
It is solely the police who choose which neighborhoods

4703
05:43:23,220 --> 05:43:25,220
to put sensors in.

4704
05:43:25,220 --> 05:43:29,220
The family members that won't forget, that's retaliation.

4705
05:43:29,220 --> 05:43:31,220
That's what worries these mums.

4706
05:43:31,220 --> 05:43:34,220
Shootings lead to revenge and more shootings.

4707
05:43:34,220 --> 05:43:37,220
They spend their lives now consoling other parents

4708
05:43:37,220 --> 05:43:39,220
and trying to break that cycle.

4709
05:43:39,220 --> 05:43:42,280
I'll never be healed until I make it up there.

