10:26:18,980 --> 10:26:22,380
Something Tirunagama says he's trying to avoid.

8894
10:26:22,380 --> 10:26:26,260
We're trying our best to manage without raising prices,

8895
10:26:26,260 --> 10:26:28,580
but it's getting more challenging day by day

8896
10:26:28,580 --> 10:26:30,900
because today's prices are not the same tomorrow.

8897
10:26:30,900 --> 10:26:32,060
We can't budget.

8898
10:26:32,060 --> 10:26:34,320
Prices are increasing.

8899
10:26:34,320 --> 10:26:36,080
And it's already evident.

8900
10:26:36,080 --> 10:26:39,560
Gayan says he's delivering few orders these days.

8901
10:26:39,560 --> 10:26:44,320
Many people we spoke to told us the worst part is the uncertainty.

8902
10:26:44,320 --> 10:26:47,320
On the way to his next pickup, Gayan fills up.

8903
10:26:47,320 --> 10:26:50,120
The government has imposed fuel restrictions.

8904
10:26:50,120 --> 10:26:53,880
Motorbike riders get a weekly quota of 8 litres.

8905
10:26:53,880 --> 10:26:57,040
Half the fuel Gayan says he usually goes through.

8906
10:26:57,040 --> 10:27:01,280
Station owner Sampat Kotalavala is also dealing with uncertainty.

8907
10:27:01,280 --> 10:27:06,720
We only receive about 50% of the supplies we order.

8908
10:27:06,720 --> 10:27:10,240
And we manage these stocks according to the framework the government has given us.

8909
10:27:10,240 --> 10:27:13,360
It's not enough for some, but generally it's okay.

8910
10:27:13,360 --> 10:27:17,420
But that's for today. I can't say what tomorrow will be like.

8911
10:27:17,420 --> 10:27:19,580
There are other pressures too.

8912
10:27:19,580 --> 10:27:23,220
A long-pending electricity price increase took effect this month

8913
10:27:23,220 --> 10:27:27,040
with some bills set to go up by 25%.

8914
10:27:27,040 --> 10:27:30,680
The government has asked people to use power sparingly.

8915
10:27:30,680 --> 10:27:33,600
Ironing and washing clothes only once a week.

8916
10:27:33,600 --> 10:27:38,200
And government officers have been told to switch off air conditioners early.

8917
10:27:38,200 --> 10:27:42,000
Just as Sri Lanka is recovering from its worst economic crisis,

8918
10:27:42,000 --> 10:27:44,800
the Iran war is causing more uncertainty.

8919
10:27:44,800 --> 10:27:49,240
People are paying more for fuel, food and even public transport

8920
10:27:49,240 --> 10:27:53,960
as a conflict thousands of kilometres away since prices soaring.

8921
10:27:53,960 --> 10:27:57,760
On the road, Gayan has stopped for a cup of tea and a snack

8922
10:27:57,800 --> 10:28:01,440
that's costing him more now than it did two weeks ago.

8923
10:28:01,440 --> 10:28:05,000
But he must hurry because the next order is waiting.

8924
10:28:05,000 --> 10:28:08,420
Minna Fernandez, Al Jazeera, Colombo.

8925
10:28:08,420 --> 10:28:12,980
The Middle East conflict is also affecting workers in Indian-administered Kashmir.

8926
10:28:12,980 --> 10:28:15,180
The region relies heavily on handicrafts

8927
10:28:15,180 --> 10:28:17,700
with thousands of people working in the industry.

8928
10:28:17,700 --> 10:28:19,340
But their livelihoods are at risk

8929
10:28:19,340 --> 10:28:22,340
because at least half of their goods are sold in the Middle East.

8930
10:28:22,340 --> 10:28:26,660
And with the region stuck in a war, orders are being delayed or cancelled.

8931
10:28:26,660 --> 10:28:30,110
Lina Abu Akle reports.

8932
10:28:30,110 --> 10:28:32,710
The Kotas are one of thousands of families

8933
10:28:32,710 --> 10:28:37,550
who have been part of Kashmir's craft industry for generations.

8934
10:28:37,550 --> 10:28:41,110
They spin yarn from the wool of Himalayan chang-thangi goats

8935
10:28:41,110 --> 10:28:46,260
on traditional hand looms, creating Peshmina scarves.

8936
10:28:48,660 --> 10:28:52,300
Peshmina is not just work for us, it's our legacy and identity.

8937
10:28:52,300 --> 10:28:55,180
I am one of the thousands of women who hand-spin the yarn

8938
10:28:55,260 --> 10:28:57,980
and this spinning is the backbone of our livelihood.

8939
10:29:00,170 --> 10:29:02,810
However, their income is in jeopardy.

8940
10:29:02,810 --> 10:29:05,050
The family has reduced production

8941
10:29:05,050 --> 10:29:08,680
using only two of their four hand looms.

8942
10:29:08,680 --> 10:29:12,640
That's because at least 50% of Kashmir's handicrafts

8943
10:29:12,640 --> 10:29:14,480
are sold to the Middle East

8944
10:29:14,480 --> 10:29:18,160
and the regional conflict has led to cancellations.

8945
10:29:18,160 --> 10:29:22,800
This is impacting us a lot.

8946
10:29:22,800 --> 10:29:25,840
The work is minimal, about 90% less than usual.

8947
10:29:27,670 --> 10:29:32,030
Tausif Bhatt also comes from a family of Peshmina makers.

8948
10:29:32,030 --> 10:29:37,460
But now, he runs a company employing around 60 people.

8949
10:29:40,340 --> 10:29:44,020
If the situation remains the same and the conflict continues,

8950
10:29:44,020 --> 10:29:47,260
I think we may eventually have to shut down the business.

8951
10:29:49,720 --> 10:29:53,640
The Kashmir Chamber of Commerce says it's not only a lack of orders

8952
10:29:53,640 --> 10:29:56,840
that is a problem, but the cost of sending anything

8953
10:29:56,840 --> 10:29:58,720
has risen astronomically.

8954
10:29:58,720 --> 10:30:03,560
Nobody can send the shipments, we have the airline problems,

8955
10:30:03,560 --> 10:30:06,040
we have the by sea, there are problems.

8956
10:30:06,040 --> 10:30:12,480
And I would rather say 400,000 people are affected with this war.

8957
10:30:13,780 --> 10:30:17,580
That's a lot of families at risk of losing their livelihoods.

8958
10:30:17,620 --> 10:30:24,020
Let's take a look at some of the other stories making news.

8959
10:30:24,020 --> 10:30:28,020
In the Gaza Strip, Hamas says it will not hand over its weapons.

8960
10:30:28,020 --> 10:30:31,620
Disarmament is part of the second phase of the Gaza ceasefire plan.

8961
10:30:31,620 --> 10:30:35,300
But the armed group says calls to lay down its weapons are unacceptable,

8962
10:30:35,300 --> 10:30:39,180
especially because Palestinians continue to be targeted by Israel.

8963
10:30:39,180 --> 10:30:44,060
More than 700 have been killed since the ceasefire came into effect in October.

8964
10:30:44,060 --> 10:30:49,340
As for raising the issue of weapons in this crude manner,

8965
10:30:49,340 --> 10:30:52,300
it is nothing but a scandalous attempt by the occupation

8966
10:30:52,300 --> 10:30:55,540
to continue killing and genocide against our people,

8967
10:30:55,540 --> 10:30:58,860
which we will not accept under any circumstances.

8968
10:30:58,860 --> 10:31:01,700
We affirm that what the enemy was unable to seize from us

8969
10:31:01,700 --> 10:31:05,620
with tanks and genocide, it will not seize from us with politics

8970
10:31:05,620 --> 10:31:07,940
or at the negotiation table.

8971
10:31:07,940 --> 10:31:10,100
The occupation's aggression against our people

8972
10:31:10,100 --> 10:31:12,900
and its continued closure of the blessed Al Aqsa Mosque

8973
10:31:12,900 --> 10:31:15,380
to worshipers in an unprecedented manner

8974
10:31:15,380 --> 10:31:18,860
and the approval of the law for executing Palestinian prisoners,

8975
10:31:18,860 --> 10:31:21,100
we call upon the masses of our Palestinian people

8976
10:31:21,100 --> 10:31:23,660
in the brave West Bank, the blessed Jerusalem

8977
10:31:23,660 --> 10:31:27,760
and the occupied interior to march toward Al Aqsa Mosque.

8978
10:31:27,760 --> 10:31:29,880
Muin Rabani is a non-resident fellow

8979
10:31:29,880 --> 10:31:32,920
at the Center for Conflict and Humanitarian Studies.

8980
10:31:32,920 --> 10:31:34,720
He says Hamas's statement confirms

8981
10:31:34,720 --> 10:31:36,480
that talks to implement the second phase

8982
10:31:36,480 --> 10:31:40,260
of the Gaza ceasefire plan are deadlocked.

8983
10:31:40,300 --> 10:31:43,740
What Hamas informed the mediators

8984
10:31:43,740 --> 10:31:48,180
is that it will not discuss issues such as disarmament

8985
10:31:48,180 --> 10:31:53,180
relating to the second phase of the plan for the Gaza Strip

8986
10:31:53,900 --> 10:31:58,500
until the items of the first phase are implemented.

8987
10:31:58,500 --> 10:32:00,740
That includes a cessation of hostilities.

8988
10:32:00,740 --> 10:32:04,060
As you noted, virtual daily Israeli attacks

8989
10:32:04,060 --> 10:32:05,620
on the Gaza Strip have resulted

8990
10:32:05,620 --> 10:32:08,300
in more than 700 Palestinians killed.

8991
10:32:08,340 --> 10:32:11,340
Humanitarian aid continues to be restricted

8992
10:32:11,340 --> 10:32:14,140
and most notably this National Committee

8993
10:32:14,140 --> 10:32:16,660
for the Administration of the Gaza Strip

8994
10:32:16,660 --> 10:32:20,100
which was established by the Board of Peace

8995
10:32:20,100 --> 10:32:21,700
continues to be prohibited

8996
10:32:21,700 --> 10:32:24,420
from entering the Gaza Strip by the Israelis

8997
10:32:24,420 --> 10:32:27,220
and the Board of Peace is doing absolutely nothing

8998
10:32:27,220 --> 10:32:30,740
to ensure its ability to get in.

8999
10:32:30,740 --> 10:32:33,740
And so I think Hamas is taking two positions.

9000
10:32:33,740 --> 10:32:36,540
A, it won't discuss the second phase

9001
10:32:36,580 --> 10:32:39,500
until the first phase is properly implemented.

9002
10:32:39,500 --> 10:32:42,540
And B, when those discussions do take place,

9003
10:32:42,540 --> 10:32:46,540
it's not going to simply surrender its weapons

9004
10:32:46,540 --> 10:32:51,540
unless Israel clearly meets its own obligations as well.

9005
10:32:52,260 --> 10:32:56,180
And those are obligations that have to be consistent

9006
10:32:56,180 --> 10:32:58,220
not just with what the Board of Peace wants

9007
10:32:58,220 --> 10:33:00,580
but with the international consensus

9008
10:33:00,580 --> 10:33:03,980
and the rulings of the International Court of Justice

9009
10:33:03,980 --> 10:33:06,100
that this is an illegal occupation

9010
10:33:06,100 --> 10:33:08,100
that must end.

9011
10:33:08,100 --> 10:33:10,100
Thousands of Palestinians in Gaza

9012
10:33:10,100 --> 10:33:12,300
are still waiting for Israeli permits

9013
10:33:12,300 --> 10:33:14,700
to evacuate for medical treatment.

9014
10:33:14,700 --> 10:33:17,700
Aza Audwan and her grandson were granted a permit

9015
10:33:17,700 --> 10:33:19,020
and went to Egypt.

9016
10:33:19,020 --> 10:33:20,620
He had a congenital heart condition

9017
10:33:20,620 --> 10:33:23,420
and needed urgent surgery, but he died.

9018
10:33:23,420 --> 10:33:24,860
When Aza returned to Gaza,

9019
10:33:24,860 --> 10:33:26,620
she found her husband and children

9020
10:33:26,620 --> 10:33:28,700
had been killed in an airstrike.

9021
10:33:28,700 --> 10:33:29,820
She's now alone.

9022
10:33:29,820 --> 10:33:32,670
In this report, she shares her story.

9023
10:33:32,670 --> 10:33:35,330
Who are you, mother?

9024
10:33:35,330 --> 10:33:37,130
My brother-in-law, my brother-in-law.

9025
10:33:37,130 --> 10:33:40,250
I left Gaza with Hafideh,

9026
10:33:40,250 --> 10:33:41,410
the most secure one.

9027
10:33:41,410 --> 10:33:44,290
Hafideh was the first one to give birth to my son.

9028
10:33:44,290 --> 10:33:46,050
He had a congenital heart condition

9029
10:33:46,050 --> 10:33:47,930
and needed urgent surgery,

9030
10:33:47,930 --> 10:33:49,930
because he had a congenital heart condition

9031
10:33:49,930 --> 10:33:51,490
and had severe injuries.

9032
10:33:51,490 --> 10:33:53,450
He was suffering a lot.

9033
10:33:53,450 --> 10:33:54,730
A lot of cuts,

9034
10:33:54,730 --> 10:33:57,490
the fire and the war that we saw

9035
10:33:57,490 --> 10:33:58,730
were unbearable.

9036
10:33:58,730 --> 10:33:59,730
He needed urgent surgery,

9037
10:33:59,730 --> 10:34:01,530
but unfortunately, in Gaza,

9038
10:34:01,530 --> 10:34:04,130
there were no hospitals or hospitals.

9039
10:34:04,130 --> 10:34:07,690
No hospitals were able to treat him.

9040
10:34:07,690 --> 10:34:09,850
In the end, we were transferred to Egypt

9041
10:34:09,850 --> 10:34:13,030
and went to Egypt to treat him.

9042
10:34:13,030 --> 10:34:15,270
In the end, he died.

9043
10:34:15,270 --> 10:34:17,600
He died of a sudden death.

9044
10:34:17,600 --> 10:34:18,800
He died of a sudden death.

9045
10:34:18,800 --> 10:34:19,960
We were shocked

9046
10:34:19,960 --> 10:34:21,520
that we saw Józef after him.

9047
10:34:21,520 --> 10:34:23,520
After him, we saw most of his family.

9048
10:34:23,520 --> 10:34:25,160
I want to tell you

9049
10:34:25,160 --> 10:34:30,020
that Józef and his children were killed in the war.

9050
10:34:30,020 --> 10:34:32,940
They were all martyred.

9051
10:34:33,020 --> 10:34:36,220
I don't know what to say.

9052
10:34:36,220 --> 10:34:39,220
I don't know what to say.

9053
10:34:39,220 --> 10:34:42,010
I don't know what's in his heart.

9054
10:34:42,010 --> 10:34:43,850
My Lord, young people,

9055
10:34:43,850 --> 10:34:45,530
young people like Warda,

9056
10:34:45,530 --> 10:34:46,610
young people,

9057
10:34:46,610 --> 10:34:48,890
young people like me,

9058
10:34:48,890 --> 10:34:50,650
my children, Warda,

9059
10:34:50,650 --> 10:34:52,330
my heart,

9060
10:34:52,330 --> 10:34:54,830
they were all martyred.

9061
10:34:54,830 --> 10:34:56,910
Józef,

9062
10:34:56,910 --> 10:34:58,990
my life, my heart,

9063
10:34:58,990 --> 10:35:00,340
they were all martyred.

9064
10:35:00,340 --> 10:35:02,020
He had a big face.

9065
10:35:02,020 --> 10:35:03,660
He had a big face.

9066
10:35:03,660 --> 10:35:05,180
He had a big face.

9067
10:35:05,180 --> 10:35:06,740
He was all martyred.

9068
10:35:06,740 --> 10:35:09,180
He was all martyred.

9069
10:35:09,180 --> 10:35:18,070
He was all martyred.

9070
10:35:18,070 --> 10:35:20,270
Ukraine has struck a coal mine

9071
10:35:20,270 --> 10:35:22,190
in Russian-controlled Luhansk,

9072
10:35:22,190 --> 10:35:24,350
damaging a power substation

9073
10:35:24,350 --> 10:35:27,300
and trapping 41 workers underground.

9074
10:35:27,300 --> 10:35:29,460
That's according to a Russian-installed official

9075
10:35:29,460 --> 10:35:30,820
in the region.

9076
10:35:30,820 --> 10:35:32,660
Leonid Pesetchnik said

9077
10:35:32,660 --> 10:35:35,380
emergency crews are working to rescue the miners

9078
10:35:35,380 --> 10:35:37,340
and restore power to the site.

9079
10:35:37,340 --> 10:35:39,180
He said that the miners do have a supply

9080
10:35:39,180 --> 10:35:42,120
of drinking water.

9081
10:35:42,120 --> 10:35:44,960
Serbia says that explosives have been found

9082
10:35:44,960 --> 10:35:48,320
near a pipeline that carries Russian gas to Hungary.

9083
10:35:48,320 --> 10:35:50,280
Authorities say the discovery was made

9084
10:35:50,280 --> 10:35:54,080
outside a Serbian town near the Hungarian border.

9085
10:35:54,080 --> 10:35:55,200
It comes just a week

9086
10:35:55,200 --> 10:35:58,040
before closely watched elections in Hungary.

9087
10:35:58,040 --> 10:35:59,360
Prime Minister Viktor Orban

9088
10:35:59,360 --> 10:36:02,440
is fighting to extend his 16 years in power.

9089
10:36:02,440 --> 10:36:04,760
He's linked Ukraine to those explosives

9090
10:36:04,760 --> 10:36:08,490
without blaming Kiev directly.

9091
10:36:08,490 --> 10:36:10,050
As Christians around the world

9092
10:36:10,050 --> 10:36:11,530
mark the Easter holiday,

9093
10:36:11,530 --> 10:36:12,890
under the shadow of war,

9094
10:36:12,890 --> 10:36:15,770
religious leaders were calling for peace.

9095
10:36:15,770 --> 10:36:20,910
Sonya Gallego reports.

9096
10:36:20,910 --> 10:36:24,670
It is the most important date in the Christian calendar,

9097
10:36:24,670 --> 10:36:31,540
marked this year by both tradition and tension.

9098
10:36:31,540 --> 10:36:34,340
Addressing more than a billion Catholics worldwide

9099
10:36:34,340 --> 10:36:35,660
from the Vatican,

9100
10:36:35,660 --> 10:36:40,060
Pope Leo led his first Easter Mass as pontiff.

9101
10:36:40,060 --> 10:36:41,860
And the message from St. Peter's Square

9102
10:36:41,860 --> 10:36:45,430
was shaped by events far beyond it.

9103
10:36:45,430 --> 10:36:50,790
Death is always lurking.

9104
10:36:50,790 --> 10:36:53,350
We see it present in injustices,

9105
10:36:53,350 --> 10:36:55,190
in partisan selfishness,

9106
10:36:55,190 --> 10:36:57,110
in the oppression of the poor,

9107
10:36:57,110 --> 10:37:00,710
in the lack of attention given to the most vulnerable.

9108
10:37:00,710 --> 10:37:02,510
We see it in violence,

9109
10:37:02,510 --> 10:37:04,310
in the wounds of the world,

9110
10:37:04,310 --> 10:37:07,310
in the cry of pain that rises from every corner

9111
10:37:07,310 --> 10:37:10,830
because of the abuses that crush the weakest.

9112
10:37:10,830 --> 10:37:13,990
An appeal for mercy as the conflict in the Middle East

9113
10:37:14,030 --> 10:37:18,070
loomed over what is meant to be a celebration of renewal,

9114
10:37:18,070 --> 10:37:21,310
where despite airstrikes and destruction,

9115
10:37:21,310 --> 10:37:26,990
many felt the need to commemorate the holiday.

9116
10:37:26,990 --> 10:37:29,950
Over the weekend, the message resonated in Germany

9117
10:37:29,950 --> 10:37:32,390
in the annual Easter March in Cologne,

9118
10:37:32,390 --> 10:37:34,190
not a religious procession,

9119
10:37:34,190 --> 10:37:38,540
but a demand for an end to hostilities.

9120
10:37:38,540 --> 10:37:42,660
And in France, as the bells of Notre Dame in Paris rang out,

9121
10:37:42,660 --> 10:37:46,220
calling worshippers to mass.

9122
10:37:46,220 --> 10:37:50,100
In Lyon, thousands of adults were baptized.

9123
10:37:50,100 --> 10:37:53,460
A sign said church leaders of the search for meaning

9124
10:37:53,460 --> 10:37:56,020
in an ever more uncertain world.

9125
10:37:56,020 --> 10:37:59,270
Sonia Gallego Al Jazeera.

9126
10:37:59,270 --> 10:38:01,510
One of China's leading arts universities

9127
10:38:01,510 --> 10:38:04,710
has scrapped degrees in subjects like translation

9128
10:38:04,710 --> 10:38:07,830
and photography, saying they're a waste of resources

9129
10:38:07,830 --> 10:38:10,150
in the age of artificial intelligence.

9130
10:38:10,150 --> 10:38:12,790
The decision is now fueling debate online

9131
10:38:12,790 --> 10:38:16,670
about how far technology should be shaping education.

9132
10:38:16,670 --> 10:38:21,300
Katrina Yu reports from Beijing.

9133
10:38:21,300 --> 10:38:24,220
Alex Scher built her career in the creative industries

9134
10:38:24,220 --> 10:38:25,700
after graduating with a degree

9135
10:38:25,700 --> 10:38:28,100
in English translation and interpreting,

9136
10:38:28,100 --> 10:38:31,700
but qualifications like hers could soon disappear.

9137
10:38:31,700 --> 10:38:34,700
As some of China's biggest universities cut courses,

9138
10:38:34,700 --> 10:38:38,700
they say are being overtaken by artificial intelligence.

9139
10:38:38,700 --> 10:38:40,740
Alex says the move risks overlooking

9140
10:38:40,740 --> 10:38:42,980
the broader skills behind translation,

9141
10:38:42,980 --> 10:38:45,780
from communication to critical thinking.

9142
10:38:45,780 --> 10:38:47,580
When you translate for sure,

9143
10:38:47,580 --> 10:38:51,460
yes, AI could probably get the accuracy up

9144
10:38:51,460 --> 10:38:54,220
to almost close to perfection,

9145
10:38:54,220 --> 10:38:57,380
but there's still that personal style

9146
10:38:57,380 --> 10:38:59,940
that's always been essential in translation.

9147
10:38:59,940 --> 10:39:01,740
And when it comes to interpreting.

9148
10:39:01,740 --> 10:39:03,540
It's not just translation.

9149
