One nation that's hoping to gain

9928
11:13:30,560 --> 11:13:32,360
from the Middle East conflict is Russia,

9929
11:13:32,360 --> 11:13:34,880
the world's third biggest oil producer.

9930
11:13:34,880 --> 11:13:37,040
Higher crude prices due to this disruption

9931
11:13:37,040 --> 11:13:38,080
in the Strait of Hormuz

9932
11:13:38,080 --> 11:13:39,480
have allowed Russia to earn more

9933
11:13:39,480 --> 11:13:41,640
from its oil and gas exports.

9934
11:13:41,640 --> 11:13:44,120
The US has temporarily eased sanctions

9935
11:13:44,120 --> 11:13:46,080
on Russian oil, but the European Union

9936
11:13:46,080 --> 11:13:47,160
has refused to do that,

9937
11:13:47,160 --> 11:13:49,440
saying more revenue will embolden Russia's efforts

9938
11:13:49,440 --> 11:13:51,640
to prolong its war in Ukraine.

9939
11:13:51,640 --> 11:13:53,440
But the revised budget plans are at risk

9940
11:13:53,440 --> 11:13:55,240
following repeated Ukrainian attacks

9941
11:13:55,240 --> 11:13:57,040
on ports and oil refineries.

9942
11:13:57,040 --> 11:13:58,640
Russia has banned petrol exports

9943
11:13:58,640 --> 11:14:01,320
to protect against domestic fuel shortages.

9944
11:14:01,320 --> 11:14:04,000
So can Russia help fill the global energy gap?

9945
11:14:04,000 --> 11:14:13,540
Or is its capacity already under threat?

9946
11:14:13,540 --> 11:14:15,580
Russia is seeing a turnaround

9947
11:14:15,580 --> 11:14:16,860
in its economic prospects

9948
11:14:16,860 --> 11:14:18,380
as oil and gas prices rise

9949
11:14:18,380 --> 11:14:21,540
and its tankers benefit from US-sanctioned waivers.

9950
11:14:21,540 --> 11:14:24,020
While the European Union is holding on to sanctions,

9951
11:14:24,020 --> 11:14:25,860
is there a new appetite in Europe

9952
11:14:25,860 --> 11:14:27,740
for Russian oil and gas?

9953
11:14:27,740 --> 11:14:30,620
The increased revenues expected to help close budget holes,

9954
11:14:30,620 --> 11:14:33,580
as well as bolster Russia's war plans against Ukraine.

9955
11:14:33,580 --> 11:14:35,540
But Kyiv has accelerated its strikes

9956
11:14:35,540 --> 11:14:37,580
on Russian oil infrastructure.

9957
11:14:37,580 --> 11:14:40,060
Will Ukrainian attacks limit Moscow's ability

9958
11:14:40,060 --> 11:14:42,420
to stabilize the global energy market?

9959
11:14:42,420 --> 11:14:44,860
We have a panel of guests to discuss all this shortly,

9960
11:14:44,860 --> 11:14:47,780
but first, here's Finnton Monaghan's report.

9961
11:14:49,690 --> 11:14:52,890
The war in the Middle East has raged for more than a month.

9962
11:14:52,890 --> 11:14:55,090
Disruption to shipping through the Strait of Hormuz

9963
11:14:55,090 --> 11:14:58,930
has cut off 20% of the world's oil and gas supply.

9964
11:14:58,930 --> 11:15:01,370
Many countries are preparing for tough times,

9965
11:15:01,370 --> 11:15:03,530
but for one, the chaos could provide

9966
11:15:03,530 --> 11:15:05,970
an opportunity to come out ahead.

9967
11:15:05,970 --> 11:15:11,210
Now that the prices of our traditional exports are rising,

9968
11:15:11,210 --> 11:15:13,170
but the markets are in turmoil,

9969
11:15:13,170 --> 11:15:17,290
there may be a temptation to take advantage of the situation,

9970
11:15:17,290 --> 11:15:19,530
to generate short-term gains.

9971
11:15:19,530 --> 11:15:22,090
I would like to emphasize it once again.

9972
11:15:22,090 --> 11:15:25,920
We must exercise common sense.

9973
11:15:25,920 --> 11:15:28,840
Russia is one of the world's largest producers of oil,

9974
11:15:28,840 --> 11:15:32,480
number three behind the United States and Saudi Arabia.

9975
11:15:32,480 --> 11:15:34,280
It relies on oil and gas revenues

9976
11:15:34,280 --> 11:15:37,320
to fund around a third of its national budget.

9977
11:15:37,320 --> 11:15:43,040
Up until 2022, it provided around 10% of global supply.

9978
11:15:43,040 --> 11:15:46,600
But the war in Ukraine upended Russia's economic model.

9979
11:15:46,640 --> 11:15:48,400
Western powers imposed sanctions

9980
11:15:48,400 --> 11:15:50,520
that closed off many key markets.

9981
11:15:50,520 --> 11:15:54,080
Russia continued to sell oil to partners like China and India,

9982
11:15:54,080 --> 11:15:56,360
but had to do so at a discount.

9983
11:15:56,360 --> 11:15:59,240
The Iran War has changed that arithmetic.

9984
11:15:59,240 --> 11:16:00,840
Fuel prices are surging,

9985
11:16:00,840 --> 11:16:02,680
as countries rushed outbid each other

9986
11:16:02,680 --> 11:16:05,160
to access suddenly limited supply.

9987
11:16:05,160 --> 11:16:08,190
The result has been a win-full for Russia.

9988
11:16:08,190 --> 11:16:11,750
Years of war and sanctions had squeezed Russia's finances.

9989
11:16:11,750 --> 11:16:14,470
Oil and gas revenues were down to $10 billion

9990
11:16:14,470 --> 11:16:16,310
in the first two months of the year,

9991
11:16:16,310 --> 11:16:20,750
a 47% drop compared to the same period in 2025.

9992
11:16:20,750 --> 11:16:23,470
The Kremlin was reportedly planning a 10% cut

9993
11:16:23,470 --> 11:16:25,710
to all non-security spending.

9994
11:16:25,710 --> 11:16:28,350
But now, analysts predict Russia could gain

9995
11:16:28,350 --> 11:16:32,510
an additional $45 billion in budget revenue this year.

9996
11:16:32,510 --> 11:16:35,110
If the war drags on for more than six months,

9997
11:16:35,110 --> 11:16:38,790
that could reach as high as $151 billion,

9998
11:16:38,790 --> 11:16:40,710
enough to replenish state coffers

9999
11:16:40,710 --> 11:16:44,210
and maintain war spending for years to come.

10000
11:16:44,210 --> 11:16:46,450
The need to stabilize global energy markets

10001
11:16:46,450 --> 11:16:48,610
has also benefited Russia.

10002
11:16:48,610 --> 11:16:51,090
The US loosened sanctions on Russian oil

10003
11:16:51,090 --> 11:16:52,610
that's already at sea,

10004
11:16:52,610 --> 11:16:55,730
freeing up around 100 million barrels for sale.

10005
11:16:55,730 --> 11:16:58,090
Europe shifted away from Russian energy,

10006
11:16:58,090 --> 11:17:00,210
but the current crisis has created pressure

10007
11:17:00,210 --> 11:17:02,130
to reverse that policy.

10008
11:17:02,130 --> 11:17:05,490
So far, the EU is resisting that temptation.

10009
11:17:05,490 --> 11:17:08,290
We see that the Russian economy is not doing well,

10010
11:17:08,290 --> 11:17:12,810
even the oil price hike is not helping them

10011
11:17:12,810 --> 11:17:14,690
as much as they need.

10012
11:17:14,690 --> 11:17:17,410
They have huge issues with recruitment

10013
11:17:17,410 --> 11:17:20,370
of new soldiers to their army.

10014
11:17:20,370 --> 11:17:23,250
So we have to see that this is the picture

10015
11:17:23,250 --> 11:17:25,170
that we can't give up now

10016
11:17:25,170 --> 11:17:28,650
with actually have to increase the pressure.

10017
11:17:28,650 --> 11:17:32,170
Ukraine is also keen to undermine Russia's advantage.

10018
11:17:32,170 --> 11:17:35,450
It stepped up attacks on oil export hubs.

10019
11:17:35,450 --> 11:17:38,170
40% of Russia's oil export capability

10020
11:17:38,170 --> 11:17:39,450
is now compromised,

10021
11:17:39,450 --> 11:17:41,370
according to the Reuters news agency.

10022
11:17:43,210 --> 11:17:45,050
Kiev strikes at damaged refineries,

10023
11:17:45,050 --> 11:17:47,650
causing fuel shortages in some regions.

10024
11:17:47,650 --> 11:17:51,570
Moscow is responded by imposing an export ban on petrol.

10025
11:17:51,570 --> 11:17:53,770
Ukraine's allies have been seizing tankers

10026
11:17:53,770 --> 11:17:56,170
belonging to the so-called Russian shadow fleet,

10027
11:17:56,170 --> 11:17:58,810
carrying oil and violation of sanctions.

10028
11:17:58,810 --> 11:18:00,690
Russia has downplayed the impact,

10029
11:18:00,690 --> 11:18:04,090
but warned it could make the global energy crisis worse.

10030
11:18:07,180 --> 11:18:08,820
Ukraine's attacks are creating,

10031
11:18:08,820 --> 11:18:10,220
amongst other things,

10032
11:18:10,220 --> 11:18:12,620
some entirely temporary difficulties,

10033
11:18:12,620 --> 11:18:15,020
but those could lead to greater price rises

10034
11:18:15,020 --> 11:18:16,740
and even deeper crisis,

10035
11:18:16,740 --> 11:18:20,050
including in the European Union and Britain.

10036
11:18:20,050 --> 11:18:21,930
Russia appears positioned to benefit

10037
11:18:21,930 --> 11:18:23,770
from the crisis in the Gulf,

10038
11:18:23,770 --> 11:18:26,130
and the longer the disruption continues,

10039
11:18:26,130 --> 11:18:28,450
the more it stands to gain.

10040
11:18:28,450 --> 11:18:32,860
Vinten Monaghan, Al Jazeera, for Counting the Cost.

10041
11:18:32,860 --> 11:18:34,540
Let's dive deeper into this.

10042
11:18:34,540 --> 11:18:36,700
Joining us from Moscow is a Russian energy expert

10043
11:18:36,700 --> 11:18:39,100
of Vyacheslav Mishenko in London.

10044
11:18:39,100 --> 11:18:39,940
We have John Lov.

10045
11:18:39,940 --> 11:18:41,220
He is head of policy

10046
11:18:41,220 --> 11:18:43,580
at the Think Tank New Eurasian Strategy Centre

10047
11:18:43,580 --> 11:18:45,620
and has previously worked with NATO

10048
11:18:45,620 --> 11:18:47,420
and the Russian oil and gas industry,

10049
11:18:47,420 --> 11:18:49,900
and in Berlin is Maria Pashtukova.

10050
11:18:49,900 --> 11:18:53,700
She's an expert in energy geopolitics and diplomacy,

10051
11:18:53,700 --> 11:18:56,540
as well as the program lead at E3G.

10052
11:18:56,540 --> 11:18:57,940
It's an independent think tank

10053
11:18:57,940 --> 11:19:00,580
focusing on energy policies globally.

10054
11:19:00,580 --> 11:19:02,900
First of all, Vyacheslav, let's start off with you.

10055
11:19:02,900 --> 11:19:04,300
How, what kind of state

10056
11:19:04,300 --> 11:19:07,810
is the Russian oil industry actually in?

10057
11:19:07,810 --> 11:19:12,290
Yes, well, actually, so for a decade or so,

10058
11:19:12,290 --> 11:19:15,850
Russian oil industry was a subject of coordination.

10059
11:19:15,850 --> 11:19:18,330
I'm talking about the production of oil, of course,

10060
11:19:18,330 --> 11:19:21,090
within the OPEC Plus platform.

10061
11:19:21,090 --> 11:19:25,210
And now I think because of the situation in the Gulf,

10062
11:19:25,210 --> 11:19:28,770
so this agreement and actually restrictions on production,

10063
11:19:28,770 --> 11:19:30,330
they don't work anymore.

10064
11:19:30,330 --> 11:19:33,370
So I think, so the production is there.

10065
11:19:34,250 --> 11:19:37,730
So Russia possesses some additional volumes to produce

10066
11:19:37,730 --> 11:19:40,250
and there are two crudes actually,

10067
11:19:40,250 --> 11:19:42,810
two market crudes like euros,

10068
11:19:42,810 --> 11:19:46,530
which normally should go to the west side

10069
11:19:46,530 --> 11:19:49,250
and actually ESPO, ESPO,

10070
11:19:49,250 --> 11:19:52,010
calls after the pipeline,

10071
11:19:52,010 --> 11:19:53,970
East Siberia Pacific Ocean,

10072
11:19:53,970 --> 11:19:57,570
which goes to the Pacific Ocean, actually.

10073
11:19:57,570 --> 11:19:59,370
I think that's the,

10074
11:20:00,000 --> 11:20:06,640
direction Russia could increase because the demand is in Asia-Pacific and actually South

10075
11:20:06,640 --> 11:20:14,320
and East Asia, and it amounts around 80 million tons a year, and in general I think Russia

10076
11:20:14,320 --> 11:20:20,280
could add and ship additional routes to this direction.

10077
11:20:20,280 --> 11:20:26,360
On top of that, there are some cargoes which were a subject of sanctions already

10078
11:20:26,360 --> 11:20:32,160
on the routes, and I think of fuck, and in general the American administration gave permission

10079
11:20:32,160 --> 11:20:35,680
to key buyers like India to get the screwed.

10080
11:20:35,680 --> 11:20:43,040
It was about 50 million barrels, I think, which already sold in the first month.

10081
11:20:43,040 --> 11:20:50,920
And the permission, if I'm not wrong, is 11th of April will be shut.

10082
11:20:50,920 --> 11:20:55,400
So I'm not sure about whether they go and prolongate it, but if so, Russia could

10083
11:20:55,440 --> 11:20:58,720
deliver more Euro-screwed to India as well.

10084
11:20:58,720 --> 11:21:02,760
Maria, the same question for you, and of course we're looking at all this in light of many

10085
11:21:02,760 --> 11:21:06,560
attacks by Ukrainian drones on Russian oil facilities.

10086
11:21:06,560 --> 11:21:09,140
Yes, sure.

10087
11:21:09,140 --> 11:21:14,020
So what I would say is that the serious bottleneck right now is the availability of freshers,

10088
11:21:14,020 --> 11:21:16,380
export infrastructure.

10089
11:21:16,380 --> 11:21:21,500
Its exports fell already by about 400,000 barrels month to month in February.

10090
11:21:21,500 --> 11:21:24,460
That was even before the latest Baltic escalation.

10091
11:21:24,460 --> 11:21:29,420
And then the March attacks on Primorsk and East Luga hit the export system much more directly.

10092
11:21:29,420 --> 11:21:34,020
What we're looking at is approximately 40% of Russia's crude export capacity that has

10093
11:21:34,020 --> 11:21:39,540
been affected, not of all of that taken out completely, but some parts of it.

10094
11:21:39,540 --> 11:21:44,180
So the Russia's Western export system has been impaired quite a bit.

10095
11:21:44,180 --> 11:21:49,780
And given that there are export constraints on the eastern track, because most of the

10096
11:21:49,780 --> 11:21:56,820
capacity towards the east is already at maximum or close to maximum, it is a big question

10097
11:21:56,820 --> 11:22:01,900
whether Russia will be able to boost its exports at all, will have actually to cut production

10098
11:22:01,900 --> 11:22:05,980
both of crude and petroleum products, because particularly the Western ports were

10099
11:22:05,980 --> 11:22:10,580
responsible for some exports of Russian petroleum products.

10100
11:22:10,580 --> 11:22:16,460
In that respect, even if Russia were able to boost its production and it has never

10101
11:22:16,460 --> 11:22:22,060
been a big swing state, so a boosting production in a short, short-distance demand has never

10102
11:22:22,060 --> 11:22:25,060
been Russia's forte, even if it would have been possible.

10103
11:22:25,060 --> 11:22:28,340
It's a big question whether it will be able to get it out.

10104
11:22:28,340 --> 11:22:31,780
We do not know the extent of the damage done fully yet.

10105
11:22:31,780 --> 11:22:36,660
We might be looking at several weeks, might be looking at some parts of that capacity

10106
11:22:36,660 --> 11:22:39,580
being out of operation for some months.

10107
11:22:39,580 --> 11:22:46,100
So I would say Russia cannot really meaningfully help offset the global energy disruptions

10108
11:22:46,100 --> 11:22:53,300
in particularly on oil in the short or mid-term, because what we're looking at is

10109
11:22:53,300 --> 11:22:58,660
it is not all of the 20 million barrels a day that normally exit hormones that are locked right now.

10110
11:22:58,660 --> 11:23:04,660
I think we're looking at about 9 to 10 million barrels a day of global oil shorted,

10111
11:23:04,660 --> 11:23:10,220
because a significant part of that is still getting out via land and sea.

10112
11:23:10,220 --> 11:23:15,620
But also Iran keeps exporting almost at capacity to China.

10113
11:23:15,660 --> 11:23:18,180
But still, it's about 10 million barrels a day.

10114
11:23:18,180 --> 11:23:21,500
It's about 10% of global oil demand.

10115
11:23:21,500 --> 11:23:26,540
Russia can in no meaningful way replace these cargoes.

10116
11:23:26,540 --> 11:23:29,420
John, two quite opposite views there.

10117
11:23:29,420 --> 11:23:31,530
What's your take?

10118
11:23:31,530 --> 11:23:37,250
Well, my take is that Russia is going to struggle to increase production significantly,

10119
11:23:37,250 --> 11:23:39,010
both in short-term and mid-term.

10120
11:23:39,010 --> 11:23:42,010
Short-term, I think probably over the next year, it could do another,

10121
11:23:42,010 --> 11:23:45,570
probably additional 5%, something like that.

10122
11:23:45,610 --> 11:23:48,090
It would then have to drill a lot more wells.

10123
11:23:48,090 --> 11:23:52,690
And then you'd be looking maybe at another 5% in a year's time.

10124
11:23:52,690 --> 11:23:56,410
So I tend to agree with you that Russia's ability to fill the gap here

10125
11:23:56,410 --> 11:23:58,690
is going to be somewhat limited.

10126
11:23:58,690 --> 11:24:02,730
And indeed, we've got also the fact, as Maria was saying,

10127
11:24:02,730 --> 11:24:05,810
that these export terminals have been damaged recently.

10128
11:24:05,810 --> 11:24:08,330
It's difficult to know how long it's going to take to repair those,

10129
11:24:08,330 --> 11:24:11,930
but there's certainly going to be some short-term impact.

10130
11:24:11,930 --> 11:24:15,970
So I think relying on Russia to be a sort of swing supplier

10131
11:24:15,970 --> 11:24:19,490
in these conditions is really rather optimistic.

10132
11:24:19,490 --> 11:24:22,210
Yeah, just your take on this.

10133
11:24:22,210 --> 11:24:26,330
I mean, the thing is that Russia produces the right kind of oil as well.

10134
11:24:26,330 --> 11:24:30,520
And how much of that is the spare capacity?

10135
11:24:30,520 --> 11:24:33,320
I'm not sure about whether I can answer this question,

10136
11:24:33,320 --> 11:24:37,480
but I would like to stress that since we're talking about the volumes,

10137
11:24:37,480 --> 11:24:42,280
I think the strategy at the moment shouldn't be just about the volume,

10138
11:24:42,600 --> 11:24:47,680
because economically, I think we, I mean, like Russian producer,

10139
11:24:47,680 --> 11:24:52,280
so we don't need to satisfy all the demands.

10140
11:24:52,280 --> 11:24:58,520
So I think the key element of this is the economic efficiency of the trade

10141
11:24:58,520 --> 11:25:01,160
because the crude and the special Russian crude

10142
11:25:01,160 --> 11:25:03,960
is now so because of the spread,

10143
11:25:03,960 --> 11:25:08,080
because of the physical markets and future market spread.

10144
11:25:08,080 --> 11:25:12,080
So the physical volumes are being traded with the premium now.

10145
11:25:12,080 --> 11:25:17,240
And I think Russia could gain and actually sell probably

10146
11:25:17,240 --> 11:25:20,880
not too many destinations and not the big volume of crude,

10147
11:25:20,880 --> 11:25:23,640
but with a high economic efficiency,

10148
11:25:23,640 --> 11:25:27,400
I think getting more commercial value of this.

10149
11:25:27,400 --> 11:25:31,200
So I think this is the strategy we should bear in our minds.

10150
11:25:32,000 --> 11:25:34,960
John, so let's just turn it this other way.

10151
11:25:34,960 --> 11:25:40,240
Is Europe actually reconsidering the use of oil from Russia?

10152
11:25:40,320 --> 11:25:44,320
And that would go really against the grain for many countries in Europe.

10153
11:25:44,320 --> 11:25:46,600
I'm not including the likes here of, let's say, Hungary.

10154
11:25:47,650 --> 11:25:52,410
Well, the European Union is committed to phasing out its

10155
11:25:53,570 --> 11:25:58,530
fossil fuel imports from Russia over the next year, 18 months.

10156
11:25:59,250 --> 11:26:02,210
Now, this this crisis is certainly,

10157
11:26:02,210 --> 11:26:05,010
I think, going to concentrate minds in some European capitals.

10158
11:26:05,530 --> 11:26:08,650
The I think probably major attraction

10159
11:26:08,690 --> 11:26:12,450
might be to import additional Russian gas.

10160
11:26:12,450 --> 11:26:14,970
And Russia has still been exporting gas to Europe

10161
11:26:15,170 --> 11:26:20,370
since the start of the war in Ukraine, but much, much reduced volumes.

10162
11:26:21,730 --> 11:26:23,050
You know, before the war started,

10163
11:26:23,050 --> 11:26:28,130
it was what up as high as, you know, 180 billion cubic meters per year.

10164
11:26:28,530 --> 11:26:31,210
And last year, I think it was down to about 18.

10165
11:26:31,210 --> 11:26:33,690
So there's been a sort of dramatic change here.

10166
11:26:34,370 --> 11:26:38,610
That's that's pipeline gas and still some significant volume

10167
11:26:38,730 --> 11:26:40,890
of liquefied natural gas, LNG.

10168
11:26:41,370 --> 11:26:44,450
But I suspect that some European countries

10169
11:26:44,450 --> 11:26:46,890
are really going to start to feel the pinch next winter

10170
11:26:46,890 --> 11:26:48,930
if this crisis persists.

10171
11:26:49,290 --> 11:26:51,650
So that question will certainly be opened up again.

10172
11:26:52,050 --> 11:26:55,010
But then we come up against the question of how to manage

