is correctly handling this war specifically.

10682
11:52:19,640 --> 11:52:23,640
We are talking about closure of educational facilities.

10683
11:52:23,640 --> 11:52:26,840
These, some classrooms have been hit

10684
11:52:26,840 --> 11:52:28,800
according to the Israeli estimates.

10685
11:52:28,800 --> 11:52:32,280
We are talking about the disrupted flight system

10686
11:52:32,280 --> 11:52:34,320
that where many Israelis cannot travel.

10687
11:52:34,320 --> 11:52:39,320
So wherever you look, you see this war affecting life

10688
11:52:39,480 --> 11:52:41,720
in Israel with no clear end inside

10689
11:52:41,720 --> 11:52:43,480
while the politicians at the same time

10690
11:52:43,480 --> 11:52:46,160
are still interested in maintaining this world

10691
11:52:46,160 --> 11:52:47,440
a bit longer.

10692
11:52:47,440 --> 11:52:50,400
Nida, you told us earlier that at the start of the war

10693
11:52:50,400 --> 11:52:53,280
there was overwhelming public support for the war in Israel

10694
11:52:53,280 --> 11:52:55,240
to the tune of about 80% of Israelis

10695
11:52:55,240 --> 11:52:58,920
who supported this war effort against Iran.

10696
11:52:58,920 --> 11:53:00,360
But now five weeks in

10697
11:53:00,360 --> 11:53:02,440
and people are still living under constant threat.

10698
11:53:02,440 --> 11:53:04,000
You told us about the school closures.

10699
11:53:04,000 --> 11:53:05,960
You told us about people going in the bunkers

10700
11:53:05,960 --> 11:53:08,760
and needing to shelter on a regular basis.

10701
11:53:08,760 --> 11:53:12,760
Is it possible to assess how much patience

10702
11:53:12,760 --> 11:53:19,020
Israelis still have for this war?

10703
11:53:19,020 --> 11:53:22,100
Also, all that patience is definitely being tested

10704
11:53:22,100 --> 11:53:24,380
not just by the continuation of the war

10705
11:53:24,380 --> 11:53:28,300
but the nature of the missiles being fired into Israel.

10706
11:53:28,300 --> 11:53:30,420
Now we are talking about a prime minister

10707
11:53:30,420 --> 11:53:32,940
who promised to change the regime,

10708
11:53:32,940 --> 11:53:34,900
to topple it in the beginning of the war.

10709
11:53:34,900 --> 11:53:37,220
But now he's saying, you know what?

10710
11:53:37,220 --> 11:53:40,460
Maybe we managed to limit Iran's existential threat

10711
11:53:40,460 --> 11:53:42,460
against us but not really stop

10712
11:53:42,460 --> 11:53:45,220
all of its ballistic missiles being sent our way.

10713
11:53:45,220 --> 11:53:47,140
This is not a good answer for Israelis

10714
11:53:47,140 --> 11:53:49,820
who have been tolerating this war,

10715
11:53:49,820 --> 11:53:52,380
tolerating this pain because they believe

10716
11:53:52,380 --> 11:53:54,580
that that will lead to better results later.

10717
11:53:54,580 --> 11:53:57,260
But now they are questioning their government's ability

10718
11:53:57,260 --> 11:53:58,540
to run this war effectively.

10719
11:53:58,540 --> 11:54:00,500
And there are those who are questioning,

10720
11:54:00,500 --> 11:54:02,220
are we waging a war because Netanyahu

10721
11:54:02,220 --> 11:54:04,460
wants to avoid corruption trials?

10722
11:54:04,460 --> 11:54:06,420
Are we doing that because he wants to win

10723
11:54:06,420 --> 11:54:08,180
the elections later this year?

10724
11:54:08,180 --> 11:54:11,820
These questions are testing what we've been reporting

10725
11:54:11,820 --> 11:54:16,940
in the past of 80% support of the war amongst Israelis,

10726
11:54:16,940 --> 11:54:18,220
a highly militarized society,

10727
11:54:18,220 --> 11:54:20,620
a society that has always seen Iran as a threat.

10728
11:54:20,620 --> 11:54:23,100
But now they're saying that maybe the government

10729
11:54:23,100 --> 11:54:26,620
is not achieving the war goals it's promised its people to.

10730
11:54:26,620 --> 11:54:29,100
And at the same time, they are questioning

10731
11:54:29,100 --> 11:54:30,140
whether Netanyahu is doing it

10732
11:54:30,180 --> 11:54:32,740
for his own political agenda.

10733
11:54:32,740 --> 11:54:37,180
So that test, that number is diminishing

10734
11:54:37,180 --> 11:54:39,100
the support of the war, we can see it.

10735
11:54:39,100 --> 11:54:42,300
And we've seen people taking to the streets of Tel Aviv

10736
11:54:42,300 --> 11:54:46,500
requiring and calling and demanding an end of this war.

10737
11:54:46,500 --> 11:54:48,780
Of course, for the political leadership, for the army,

10738
11:54:48,780 --> 11:54:50,060
they still have more time to go.

10739
11:54:50,060 --> 11:54:52,060
And there's also this interest in separating

10740
11:54:52,060 --> 11:54:54,940
between the front with Iran and the front with Hezbollah

10741
11:54:54,940 --> 11:54:58,140
as the army says, even if the war with Iran stops,

10742
11:54:58,140 --> 11:55:01,020
they will continue their battle against Hezbollah.

10743
11:55:01,020 --> 11:55:03,180
You know, Abraham reporting from Ramallah.

10744
11:55:03,180 --> 11:55:06,770
Thank you very much, Nitta.

10745
11:55:06,770 --> 11:55:08,570
And the threat of escalation in Iran

10746
11:55:08,570 --> 11:55:11,530
has put the Gulf region directly in the line of fire.

10747
11:55:11,530 --> 11:55:13,370
Health authorities in Kuwait report

10748
11:55:13,370 --> 11:55:15,250
that six people have been injured

10749
11:55:15,250 --> 11:55:18,970
after debris from a missile landed in a residential area.

10750
11:55:18,970 --> 11:55:21,970
Al Jazeera's Malik Trena is in Kuwait city.

10751
11:55:21,970 --> 11:55:23,450
Malik, you're monitoring developments

10752
11:55:23,450 --> 11:55:24,450
across the region.

10753
11:55:24,450 --> 11:55:26,050
Kuwait has been particularly hard.

10754
11:55:26,050 --> 11:55:27,450
It was yesterday, but it's also,

10755
11:55:27,450 --> 11:55:29,850
as we just reported today, what are you seeing?

10756
11:55:33,380 --> 11:55:34,220
Yeah, that's right.

10757
11:55:34,220 --> 11:55:36,500
Well, throughout the night and this morning,

10758
11:55:36,500 --> 11:55:39,420
the alarm sounded here in Kuwait three times.

10759
11:55:39,420 --> 11:55:41,940
We now know from the Ministry of Health

10760
11:55:41,940 --> 11:55:45,580
that those people were injured

10761
11:55:45,580 --> 11:55:47,460
in the northern part of the country

10762
11:55:47,460 --> 11:55:49,260
in a residential area.

10763
11:55:49,260 --> 11:55:52,460
The ministry is now saying that they've all been treated

10764
11:55:52,460 --> 11:55:55,820
and are doing very well now.

10765
11:55:55,820 --> 11:55:57,580
But we've also seen attacks across the region.

10766
11:55:57,580 --> 11:56:01,020
In the UAE, one person was injured

10767
11:56:01,020 --> 11:56:04,980
in an attack in the industrial city of Abu Dhabi.

10768
11:56:04,980 --> 11:56:06,580
He was a Ghanaian national

10769
11:56:06,580 --> 11:56:08,540
from debris from an interception.

10770
11:56:08,540 --> 11:56:10,140
You know, what we've learned now

10771
11:56:10,140 --> 11:56:14,100
is that the debris from these successful interceptions

10772
11:56:14,100 --> 11:56:18,420
can be dangerous and sometimes quite deadly.

10773
11:56:18,420 --> 11:56:20,980
In Saudi Arabia, the Ministry of Defense saying...

10774
11:56:20,980 --> 11:56:24,790
24 hours on, what's the damage assessment

10775
11:56:24,790 --> 11:56:29,550
from those attacks?

10776
11:56:29,550 --> 11:56:31,710
Well, according to what we understand,

10777
11:56:31,710 --> 11:56:33,870
there are still some of these fires

10778
11:56:33,870 --> 11:56:36,430
that are ongoing with civil defense teams

10779
11:56:36,430 --> 11:56:38,510
trying to put them out.

10780
11:56:38,510 --> 11:56:40,030
Some of the fires,

10781
11:56:40,030 --> 11:56:42,950
including the finance ministry building

10782
11:56:42,950 --> 11:56:44,590
and the oil complex,

10783
11:56:44,590 --> 11:56:47,350
those fires, the authorities said, were put out.

10784
11:56:47,350 --> 11:56:49,950
But numerous fires.

10785
11:56:49,950 --> 11:56:52,630
I'm talking about several different locations.

10786
11:56:52,630 --> 11:56:56,310
The petrol chemical company, also oil facilities.

10787
11:56:56,310 --> 11:56:58,030
Several fires were put out there.

10788
11:56:58,030 --> 11:57:01,670
Some operational units were taken offline.

10789
11:57:01,710 --> 11:57:05,550
You talked about the water and powered infrastructure here.

10790
11:57:05,550 --> 11:57:07,550
The Ezur water plant,

10791
11:57:07,550 --> 11:57:10,470
which is one of the places that was targeted.

10792
11:57:10,470 --> 11:57:12,830
It's one of the biggest desalination plants

10793
11:57:12,830 --> 11:57:15,030
in the entire Middle East.

10794
11:57:15,030 --> 11:57:16,390
You know, water infrastructure,

10795
11:57:16,390 --> 11:57:17,870
extremely important in the Gulf,

10796
11:57:17,870 --> 11:57:19,430
but here in Kuwait,

10797
11:57:19,430 --> 11:57:21,510
eight desalination plants accumulate

10798
11:57:21,510 --> 11:57:25,670
for more than 90% of the drinking water.

10799
11:57:25,670 --> 11:57:27,190
So, you know, for officials here,

10800
11:57:27,190 --> 11:57:31,350
that's a red line that continuously is being crossed.

10801
11:57:31,350 --> 11:57:32,710
This was the fourth time

10802
11:57:32,710 --> 11:57:36,270
that a desalination plant was hit here in Kuwait.

10803
11:57:36,270 --> 11:57:39,150
And what we've seen in the last couple of days

10804
11:57:39,150 --> 11:57:40,990
is that these Iranian drones

10805
11:57:40,990 --> 11:57:43,190
have been able to get through

10806
11:57:43,190 --> 11:57:45,110
the Kuwaiti air defense system.

10807
11:57:45,110 --> 11:57:47,350
So, as this looming deadline

10808
11:57:47,350 --> 11:57:49,350
that's been imposed by Donald Trump,

10809
11:57:49,350 --> 11:57:51,790
you know, we edge closer and closer,

10810
11:57:51,790 --> 11:57:54,550
people here have become extremely concerned.

10811
11:57:54,550 --> 11:57:55,350
I think, you know,

10812
11:57:55,350 --> 11:57:58,390
for Gulf officials across the region,

10813
11:57:58,390 --> 11:57:59,750
you know, people are trying,

10814
11:58:00,030 --> 11:58:02,630
officials want to de-escalate the situation.

10815
11:58:02,630 --> 11:58:04,550
We heard from the Omanians yesterday

10816
11:58:04,550 --> 11:58:07,270
that they're in talks with the Iranians

10817
11:58:07,270 --> 11:58:09,590
to come up with some kind of mechanism

10818
11:58:09,590 --> 11:58:11,870
to ensure passage through the Strait of Hormuz.

10819
11:58:11,870 --> 11:58:13,990
I think what officials here in the Gulf

10820
11:58:13,990 --> 11:58:16,350
will try to relate to President Trump is,

10821
11:58:16,350 --> 11:58:18,350
look, the Iranians are playing ball.

10822
11:58:18,350 --> 11:58:19,950
They're trying to negotiate.

10823
11:58:19,950 --> 11:58:21,550
Let's de-escalate the situation.

10824
11:58:21,550 --> 11:58:23,870
Let's move this deadline

10825
11:58:23,870 --> 11:58:26,110
so we can find a diplomatic path,

10826
11:58:26,110 --> 11:58:29,430
a solution that will bring long-term stability

10827
11:58:29,430 --> 11:58:31,430
here in this entire region.

10828
11:58:31,430 --> 11:58:33,830
Malik Trena reporting from Kuwait City.

10829
11:58:33,830 --> 11:58:36,140
Thank you very much, Malik.

10830
11:58:36,140 --> 11:58:37,820
And US President Donald Trump

10831
11:58:37,820 --> 11:58:40,220
has been giving Iran shifting deadlines

10832
11:58:40,220 --> 11:58:42,060
to reopen the Strait of Hormuz.

10833
11:58:42,060 --> 11:58:43,340
That is as Iran insists

10834
11:58:43,340 --> 11:58:45,660
that the key waterway isn't actually closed

10835
11:58:45,660 --> 11:58:49,140
and that only ships that belong to its enemies

10836
11:58:49,140 --> 11:58:50,860
are barred from passage.

10837
11:58:50,860 --> 11:58:53,740
Trump issued his first ultimatum on March 21st.

10838
11:58:53,740 --> 11:58:56,260
He threatened at the time to bomb Iran's power plants

10839
11:58:56,260 --> 11:58:59,100
if the Strait wasn't reopened within 48 hours,

10840
11:58:59,100 --> 11:59:01,700
but he later extended that deadline by five days,

10841
11:59:01,700 --> 11:59:04,140
claiming that negotiations were underway

10842
11:59:04,140 --> 11:59:05,740
and were going well.

10843
11:59:05,740 --> 11:59:07,820
Trump issued a new deadline on March 26th

10844
11:59:07,820 --> 11:59:09,900
that that time he gave Iran 10 days

10845
11:59:09,900 --> 11:59:13,730
or until the evening of April 6th to reopen the Strait.

10846
11:59:13,730 --> 11:59:16,810
Trump issued his latest Hormuz threat on Sunday.

10847
11:59:16,810 --> 11:59:17,810
That's yesterday,

10848
11:59:17,810 --> 11:59:20,210
after vowing to bomb power plants and bridges

10849
11:59:20,210 --> 11:59:22,050
if Tehran doesn't comply.

10850
11:59:22,050 --> 11:59:23,330
He posted what appears to be

10851
11:59:23,330 --> 11:59:26,930
a Tuesday 8 p.m. Eastern, that's US time,

10852
11:59:26,970 --> 11:59:29,290
8 p.m. Eastern deadline for a deal.

10853
11:59:29,290 --> 11:59:31,570
So that brings us to Wednesday

10854
11:59:31,570 --> 11:59:33,170
in the early hours of Wednesday morning,

10855
11:59:33,170 --> 11:59:34,930
Iran time for that to happen.

10856
11:59:34,930 --> 11:59:37,250
I'm joined in the studio by Mohammed al-Mastri,

10857
11:59:37,250 --> 11:59:39,370
professor of media studies at the Doha Institute

10858
11:59:39,370 --> 11:59:42,410
for Graduate Studies and in Moruya in Australia.

10859
11:59:42,410 --> 11:59:44,210
We are joined by Michael Shubridge,

10860
11:59:44,210 --> 11:59:46,490
director of strategic analysis Australia,

10861
11:59:46,490 --> 11:59:48,650
a defense and security think tank.

10862
11:59:48,650 --> 11:59:50,330
Gentlemen, thank you for joining us

10863
11:59:50,330 --> 11:59:52,730
from Australia in the studio.

10864
11:59:52,730 --> 11:59:55,690
Really the big question I think that is animating

10865
11:59:55,730 --> 11:59:57,130
all of us, certainly all the people

10866
11:59:57,130 --> 11:59:59,610
who live in the region, but far beyond as well.

10867
12:00:00,000 --> 12:00:07,510
point is, can this threat by Donald Trump actually change anything?

10868
12:00:07,510 --> 12:00:13,710
Is it conceivable that what hasn't worked for five weeks, this massive U.S. military

10869
12:00:13,710 --> 12:00:17,230
pressure on Iran and bombing campaign, hasn't worked for five weeks?

10870
12:00:17,230 --> 12:00:19,830
We were talking about that with Michael earlier.

10871
12:00:19,830 --> 12:00:24,630
Is it possible that if you escalate it, bomb the power plants, bomb the bridges, then

10872
12:00:24,630 --> 12:00:25,630
it can work?

10873
12:00:25,630 --> 12:00:28,420
Michael?

10874
12:00:28,420 --> 12:00:30,380
Cyril, I don't think so.

10875
12:00:30,380 --> 12:00:37,380
I think Donald Trump is having a hard time understanding that Iran is not working to his timeline.

10876
12:00:37,380 --> 12:00:43,460
He's used to business deals and threatening people to get a better deal.

10877
12:00:43,460 --> 12:00:45,380
This is a different problem.

10878
12:00:45,380 --> 12:00:49,980
So no, I don't think more threats will change things.

10879
12:00:49,980 --> 12:00:54,460
My real concern is this is going to lead to an escalation of the war and cause much

10880
12:00:54,460 --> 12:00:57,660
broader damage across the Gulf and in Iran.

10881
12:00:59,050 --> 12:01:00,050
I agree.

10882
12:01:00,050 --> 12:01:01,050
I agree with Michael.

10883
12:01:01,050 --> 12:01:05,010
I think if anything, it could have the opposite effect.

10884
12:01:05,010 --> 12:01:09,970
We're in effectively what Professor Robert Pape has been calling the escalation trap.

10885
12:01:09,970 --> 12:01:17,010
So when Trump, if Trump escalates, then it will kind of force the hand of the Iranians

10886
12:01:17,010 --> 12:01:22,650
to escalate themselves and then we end up in this perpetual cycle.

10887
12:01:22,650 --> 12:01:29,770
So no, I don't think that this is likely to yield the kind of result that Trump wants.

10888
12:01:29,770 --> 12:01:34,850
Now I think what Michael said at the end there of his comment is important about the

10889
12:01:34,850 --> 12:01:39,130
Gulf because this is dangerous not just for Iran and for Iranians.

10890
12:01:39,130 --> 12:01:44,610
Obviously the consequences could be catastrophic for people in Iran if Donald Trump carries

10891
12:01:44,610 --> 12:01:49,690
out his threat, but I think also for people in the Gulf because Iran has promised this

10892
12:01:49,730 --> 12:01:57,130
kind of tit for tat response and we're getting reports that there have been some, and I just

10893
12:01:57,130 --> 12:02:05,330
want to emphasize some attacks from some, perhaps Gulf countries, U.S. attacks on Iran that

10894
12:02:05,330 --> 12:02:07,170
is from these bases.

10895
12:02:07,170 --> 12:02:15,770
France 24 was able to verify footage yesterday showing missile attacks from Kuwait.

10896
12:02:15,770 --> 12:02:19,410
You all were just covering reporting from Kuwait City.

10897
12:02:19,410 --> 12:02:28,290
So that could explain why Kuwait has come under heavier fire over the past two or three weeks.

10898
12:02:28,290 --> 12:02:39,370
And again, Iran has promised to basically make the response very costly for the Gulf if

10899
12:02:39,370 --> 12:02:42,490
Donald Trump does what he promises to do.

10900
12:02:42,490 --> 12:02:49,010
Michael, off the back of mom's point there, do you see the Gulf countries or the Gulf

10901
12:02:49,130 --> 12:02:52,010
regions military posture changing?

10902
12:02:52,690 --> 12:02:55,370
Most of them have been playing defense for now.

10903
12:02:56,010 --> 12:02:59,850
Do you see them going on the offense if Iran's attacks continue?

10904
12:03:02,240 --> 12:03:08,480
That's a possibility, but I don't think it's likely because I don't think that putting

10905
12:03:08,480 --> 12:03:12,680
more bombs and missiles into Iran is going to change things.

10906
12:03:12,680 --> 12:03:15,360
That's the problem with the Israeli and American.

10907
12:03:16,530 --> 12:03:22,690
The Gulf states know that if the Americans in Israelis start broadly targeting

10908
12:03:22,690 --> 12:03:27,810
civilian infrastructure inside Iran, Iran will start broadly targeting civilian

10909
12:03:27,810 --> 12:03:32,490
infrastructure across the Gulf and in Israel, and air defenses are already

10910
12:03:32,490 --> 12:03:36,370
struggling to defend against more limited attacks.

10911
12:03:36,850 --> 12:03:42,010
So I don't think the Gulf states want to see this next escalatory step.

10912
12:03:43,190 --> 12:03:47,790
So you believe Iran has the ability to step up its attacks then because I had a

10913
12:03:47,790 --> 12:03:51,990
guest yesterday tell me, and this was from the Gulf region, tell me that

10914
12:03:51,990 --> 12:03:55,350
actually they're not really afraid of escalation from Iran because they didn't

10915
12:03:55,350 --> 12:03:59,510
feel that Iran had the ability to do more than it's already doing.

10916
12:04:01,620 --> 12:04:05,660
Well, I think that makes a mistake about the breadth of targeting.

10917
12:04:06,100 --> 12:04:10,780
So if Iran fires the number of missiles and drones, it seems to be

10918
12:04:10,780 --> 12:04:17,100
capable of, but broadens their targets to a much wider set of civilian targets,

10919
12:04:17,500 --> 12:04:21,620
then the defense problem, the air and missile defense problem becomes much

10920
12:04:21,620 --> 12:04:26,020
more difficult and more drones and missiles will get through and strike

10921
12:04:26,020 --> 12:04:27,900
more targets in the Gulf.

10922
12:04:29,040 --> 12:04:32,400
Mohamed, since you're a professor of media studies, in addition to being

10923
12:04:32,400 --> 12:04:37,560
a commentator on regional politics, what is the perception through the

10924
12:04:37,560 --> 12:04:42,440
lens of the media in the U.S. and Israel on how they're doing five weeks in?

10925
12:04:43,900 --> 12:04:48,340
Well, in the United States, the the perception is pretty negative.

10926
12:04:48,340 --> 12:04:53,460
Actually, the opinion polling data continue to be continued to be negative.

10927
12:04:53,460 --> 12:04:58,100
So if you look at this Fox News poll, which already tends to be there,

10928
12:04:58,100 --> 12:05:03,220
there tends to be a slight right leaning sampling bias on Fox News polls.

10929
12:05:03,620 --> 12:05:07,580
But they found that 64 percent of respondents believe

10930
12:05:07,580 --> 12:05:10,100
that Donald Trump is mishandling the war.

10931
12:05:10,420 --> 12:05:12,780
So that's that's quite that's quite significant.

10932
12:05:12,780 --> 12:05:17,140
A majority of Americans continue to be opposed to the war,

10933
12:05:17,140 --> 12:05:20,820
to be opposed even to the decision to go to war.

10934
12:05:21,060 --> 12:05:24,860
The vast majority of Americans are opposed to the idea of ground troops.

10935
12:05:25,100 --> 12:05:29,460
So Donald Trump's messaging hasn't hasn't really worked.

10936
12:05:30,220 --> 12:05:33,100
And so it is it is largely negative.

10937
12:05:33,260 --> 12:05:38,660
It's becoming more negative in Israel, but it's still not negative on the whole.

10938
12:05:38,660 --> 12:05:46,060
The support has dropped from roughly 95 percent to the low 70s in recent weeks.

10939
12:05:46,060 --> 12:05:47,220
And I think still strong support.

10940
12:05:47,220 --> 12:05:48,180
Still strong support.

10941
12:05:48,180 --> 12:05:53,020
And but the longer the war goes on, the the the more unpopular it will become.

10942
12:05:53,180 --> 12:05:55,660
Could I just say something about this?

10943
12:05:55,660 --> 12:06:00,420
This this idea of Iran perhaps not being able to continue

10944
12:06:00,700 --> 12:06:02,940
the war, step up its attack, step up its attack.

10945
12:06:02,940 --> 12:06:07,860
So CNN did an interesting investigation last week, and they found that

10946
12:06:08,420 --> 12:06:12,780
and they were consulting with US intelligence officials who spoke to them off the record.

10947
12:06:13,060 --> 12:06:16,340
But Iran still maintains half of its missile launchers.

10948
12:06:16,700 --> 12:06:22,100
And it is believed that they still have quite a stockpile of of missiles

10949
12:06:22,620 --> 12:06:24,380
and thousands of drones.

10950
12:06:24,380 --> 12:06:27,780
And it's also believed that they are continuing to

10951
12:06:28,780 --> 12:06:32,300
manufacture drones and and missiles at a

10952
12:06:32,820 --> 12:06:37,060
slower pace. But but it is quite likely, I mean to say,

10953
12:06:37,060 --> 12:06:40,860
it is quite likely that Iran could could carry this on for for many months.

10954
12:06:41,540 --> 12:06:43,700
That's something that Michael and I were addressing a little earlier.

10955
12:06:43,700 --> 12:06:46,740
I've got more questions for you on that, Michael, but I have to run for now.

10956
12:06:46,740 --> 12:06:47,660
But we'll speak again.

10957
12:06:47,660 --> 12:06:49,260
Thank you very much, gentlemen.

10958
12:06:49,260 --> 12:06:52,860
Michael Shubridge and Muhammad al-Masri for joining us this hour.

10959
12:06:53,180 --> 12:06:54,790
Thanks.

10960
12:06:54,790 --> 12:06:58,350
And details are emerging of the rescue of a US airman from Iran

10961
12:06:58,470 --> 12:07:01,310
after an intense 48 hour search operation.

10962
12:07:01,310 --> 12:07:04,150
The weapons systems officer had been missing since Friday

10963
12:07:04,310 --> 12:07:08,590
when the fighter jet that he was in was shot down over a remote area in southern Iran.

10964
12:07:09,070 --> 12:07:11,750
Al Jazeera's John Hendron reports from Washington, D.C.

10965
12:07:14,210 --> 12:07:17,650
It was a daring and risky mission to save an American airman

10966
12:07:17,650 --> 12:07:20,250
from becoming an Iranian prisoner of war.

10967
12:07:20,730 --> 12:07:24,370
Iranian forces search the mountainous areas of southwestern Iran

10968
12:07:24,370 --> 12:07:27,650
after an F-15E fighter jet went down on Friday.

10969
12:07:28,130 --> 12:07:29,690
It was the first time a U.S.

10970
12:07:29,690 --> 12:07:33,570
aircraft had crashed in hostile territory in the five-week old war.

10971
12:07:35,770 --> 12:07:38,650
Two Black Hawk helicopters took fire as U.S.

10972
12:07:38,650 --> 12:07:41,050
teams raced to find the missing crew member.

10973
12:07:41,410 --> 12:07:45,330
An A-10 Warthog, an air support aircraft, was also damaged,

10974
12:07:45,450 --> 12:07:47,490
its pilot ejecting over the Gulf.

10975
12:07:48,800 --> 12:07:52,680
Iran broadcast photos of what it said was debris from the fighter jet,

10976
12:07:52,680 --> 12:07:54,440
including a jump seat.

10977
12:07:54,440 --> 12:07:56,680
Although the pilot had been rescued on Friday,

10978
12:07:56,680 --> 12:08:01,680
the weapon specialist remained in hiding, evading Iranian forces for two days.

10979
12:08:02,080 --> 12:08:05,360
Finally, early on Sunday, deep in Iranian territory,

10980
12:08:05,360 --> 12:08:08,040
the U.S. search operation was successful.

10981
12:08:08,560 --> 12:08:11,760
President Donald Trump made the announcement on social media,

10982
12:08:11,760 --> 12:08:16,000
posting, we got him, saying the Colonel had been behind enemy lines

10983
12:08:16,000 --> 12:08:19,520
in the treacherous mountains of Iran being hunted by our enemies.

10984
12:08:19,920 --> 12:08:24,400
He said U.S. forces had been monitoring his location 24 hours a day

10985
12:08:24,640 --> 12:08:28,720
and sent dozens of aircraft armed with the most lethal weapons in the world

10986
12:08:28,720 --> 12:08:29,840
to retrieve him.

10987
12:08:29,840 --> 12:08:33,680
Trump added he sustained injuries, but he will be just fine.

10988
12:08:34,360 --> 12:08:38,520
A U.S. official told Al Jazeera the rescue operation began in darkness

10989
12:08:38,520 --> 12:08:41,440
but ended in an intense firefight and daylight

10990
12:08:41,800 --> 12:08:45,440
before dozens of heavily armed aircraft and hundreds of troops

10991
12:08:45,440 --> 12:08:47,480
transported the airmen out of Iran.

10992
12:08:49,140 --> 12:08:52,940
A U.S. officer in Iranian custody could have given Iran leverage,

10993
12:08:52,940 --> 12:08:56,940
as it had when Iran took U.S. hostages in 1979.

10994
12:08:58,630 --> 12:09:02,510
With that crisis averted, attention now shifts to the U.S.

10995
12:09:02,510 --> 12:09:05,470
deadline for Iran to open the Strait of Hormuz.

10996
12:09:05,710 --> 12:09:08,310
John Hendrin, Al Jazeera, Washington.

10997
12:09:10,460 --> 12:09:13,380
And Israel has carried out multiple strikes across southern Lebanon

10998
12:09:13,380 --> 12:09:17,580
and the capital Beirut, causing widespread damage and death.

10999
12:09:17,940 --> 12:09:21,740
Israeli military attacks targeted multiple areas in the Nabatae district

11000
12:09:21,820 --> 12:09:23,780
in the south. What you're seeing right now, actually,

11001
12:09:23,780 --> 12:09:28,100
are live pictures, the aftermath of a strike that just occurred,

11002
12:09:28,220 --> 12:09:30,940
again, in the Lebanese capital Beirut.

11003
12:09:31,340 --> 12:09:35,020
So at least four people were killed in a drone strike targeting a car.

11004
12:09:35,020 --> 12:09:36,660
That was the previous strike.

11005
12:09:36,660 --> 12:09:40,020
And in a separate attack in the same area, one person was killed.

11006
12:09:40,420 --> 12:09:42,780
Al Jazeera, Zayna Hodor, is in Beirut with the latest.

11007
12:09:44,890 --> 12:09:48,450
Civilians are increasingly being caught up in this conflict.

11008
12:09:48,450 --> 12:09:51,130
The attack in Beirut on Sunday, there were two.

11009
12:09:51,410 --> 12:09:55,330
One in the district of Jnech, five people were killed,

11010
12:09:55,330 --> 12:10:00,170
three Sudanese nationals, a 15 year old child

11011
12:10:00,370 --> 12:10:04,530
and the apparent target, a Hezbollah military commander.

11012
12:10:04,530 --> 12:10:07,930
So even in the so-called targeted assassination,

11013
12:10:07,930 --> 12:10:09,530
civilians are being killed.

11014
12:10:09,530 --> 12:10:12,850
In another strike in Beirut last night in Ain Saadi,

11015
12:10:12,850 --> 12:10:17,850
that's a district north of Beirut, three people were killed.

11016
12:10:18,290 --> 12:10:20,850
The missile targeted the third floor of the building

11017
12:10:20,850 --> 12:10:24,890
and these civilians were on the second floor of the building.

11018
12:10:25,290 --> 12:10:30,330
The Lebanese health ministry saying that 1,461 people have been killed,

11019
12:10:30,730 --> 12:10:32,330
4,000 people wounded.

11020
12:10:32,330 --> 12:10:36,610
That doesn't include the latest casualties this morning in Mashkara.

11021
12:10:36,610 --> 12:10:38,890
That's in West Bikar, three people killed.

11022
12:10:39,130 --> 12:10:41,050
In Farouman, a car was hit.

11023
12:10:41,050 --> 12:10:44,490
That's in the Nabati district in south Lebanon, four people killed.

11024
12:10:44,490 --> 12:10:47,650
There was another strike in Nabati, another person killed.

11025
12:10:47,930 --> 12:10:50,410
So, you know, the death toll keeps climbing.

11026
12:10:50,410 --> 12:10:53,250
And this conflict is in its sixth week.

11027
12:10:53,410 --> 12:10:55,450
The Lebanese health ministry, in its figures,

11028
12:10:55,450 --> 12:10:58,730
it doesn't differentiate between combatants and civilians.

11029
12:10:59,010 --> 12:11:02,610
But if you count the number of women, children, paramedics,

11030
12:11:02,610 --> 12:11:04,890
that's roughly 25 percent.

11031
12:11:05,130 --> 12:11:09,650
So there is increasing concern as this conflict really has no red line,

11032
12:11:09,930 --> 12:11:14,850
even though Israel may want to, you know, target a specific Hezbollah member.

11033
12:11:15,010 --> 12:11:19,650
You know, it doesn't really matter if that member is an intensely populated area.

11034
12:11:20,810 --> 12:11:24,850
The Iran War is piling pressure on Sri Lanka's fragile economy,

11035
12:11:24,850 --> 12:11:27,890
still recovering from its financial crisis of four years ago.

11036
12:11:28,330 --> 12:11:32,010
Fuel prices have surged, with petrol and diesel now being rationed.

11037
12:11:32,330 --> 12:11:35,970
As Menel Fernandez reports from Colombo, many people are struggling to cope.

11038
12:11:37,780 --> 12:11:41,940
Lasseth Gyan has worked for a food delivery company in Colombo for four years.

11039
12:11:42,340 --> 12:11:46,060
The 39-year-old's income depends on the number of deliveries he makes.

11040
12:11:46,580 --> 12:11:50,460
But restrictions on fuel and price increases caused by the Iran War

11041
12:11:50,740 --> 12:11:52,140
have affected his earnings.

11042
12:11:54,020 --> 12:11:56,820
I make around $20 a day, but I have to buy all my meals.

11043
12:11:56,820 --> 12:11:58,620
That costs more than $5 a day.

11044
12:11:58,620 --> 12:12:01,780
I use what's left for fuel, rent and to send home to my family.

11045
12:12:02,620 --> 12:12:06,660
Restaurants like this, where Gyan is picking up his first order for the day,

11046
12:12:06,820 --> 12:12:08,300
are also struggling.

11047
12:12:08,300 --> 12:12:10,380
Gas for cooking is more expensive.

11048
12:12:11,180 --> 12:12:16,460
And manager Suranga Thirunagama says good quality ingredients are difficult to find.

11049
12:12:17,390 --> 12:12:20,550
This has forced many outlets to increase their prices.

11050
12:12:20,830 --> 12:12:23,670
Something Thirunagama says he's trying to avoid.

11051
12:12:25,470 --> 12:12:28,110
We're trying our best to manage without raising prices,

11052
12:12:28,110 --> 12:12:30,270
but it's getting more challenging day by day

11053
12:12:30,390 --> 12:12:32,750
because today's prices are not the same tomorrow.

11054
12:12:32,750 --> 12:12:35,110
We can't budget. Prices are increasing.

11055
12:12:36,160 --> 12:12:40,760
And it's already evident, Gyan says he's delivering few orders these days.

11056
12:12:41,400 --> 12:12:45,520
Many people we spoke to told us the worst part is the uncertainty.

11057
12:12:46,120 --> 12:12:48,480
On the way to his next pickup, Gyan fills up.

11058
12:12:49,160 --> 12:12:51,520
The government has imposed fuel restrictions.

11059
12:12:51,960 --> 12:12:55,320
Motorbike riders get a weekly quota of 8 litres.

11060
12:12:55,680 --> 12:12:58,400
Half the fuel Gyan says he usually goes through.

11061
12:12:58,880 --> 12:13:02,840
Station owner Sampat Kotalavala is also dealing with uncertainty.

11062
12:13:05,560 --> 12:13:08,360
We only receive about 50% of the supplies we order.

11063
12:13:08,600 --> 12:13:11,920
And we manage these stocks according to the framework the government has given us.

11064
12:13:12,120 --> 12:13:14,840
It's not enough for some, but generally it's okay.

11065
12:13:15,240 --> 12:13:17,840
But that's for today. I can't say what tomorrow will be like.

11066
12:13:19,300 --> 12:13:20,740
There are other pressures too.

11067
12:13:21,460 --> 12:13:24,860
A long-pending electricity price increase took effect this month,

11068
12:13:25,140 --> 12:13:28,100
with some bills set to go up by 25%.

11069
12:13:28,950 --> 12:13:32,190
The government has asked people to use power sparingly.

11070
12:13:32,590 --> 12:13:35,190
Ironing and washing clothes only once a week.

11071
12:13:35,470 --> 12:13:39,630
And government officers have been told to switch off air conditioners early.

11072
12:13:40,110 --> 12:13:43,710
Gyan says Sri Lanka is recovering from its worst economic crisis.

11073
12:13:43,910 --> 12:13:46,430
The Iran war is causing more uncertainty.

11074
12:13:46,670 --> 12:13:50,910
People are paying more for fuel, food and even public transport,

11075
12:13:51,110 --> 12:13:55,230
as a conflict thousands of kilometres away, since prices soaring.

11076
12:13:55,830 --> 12:13:59,430
On the road, Gyan has stopped for a cup of tea and a snack

11077
12:13:59,630 --> 12:14:02,670
that's costing him more now than it did two weeks ago.

11078
12:14:03,270 --> 12:14:06,350
But he must hurry because the next order is waiting.

11079
12:14:06,870 --> 12:14:09,270
Minal Fernandez, Al Jazeera, Colombo.

11080
12:14:10,860 --> 12:14:13,420
At least 41 miners are trapped underground

11081
12:14:13,420 --> 12:14:16,940
after an attack on a coal mine in the Russian-controlled Luhansk.

11082
12:14:17,100 --> 12:14:21,140
A Russian-appointed official in the region says Ukraine was behind the strike

11083
12:14:21,460 --> 12:14:23,780
and that a power substation was damaged.

11084
12:14:24,300 --> 12:14:28,580
Emergency crews are working to rescue the miners and restore power to that site.

11085
12:14:29,720 --> 12:14:32,960
Four astronauts are hours away from becoming the first people

11086
12:14:32,960 --> 12:14:42,580
to see the dark side of the moon.

11087
12:14:42,580 --> 12:14:46,620
The Artemis II mission crew has entered the final phase of its journey,

11088
12:14:46,740 --> 12:14:49,420
preparing to loop around the far side of the moon.

11089
12:14:49,460 --> 12:14:53,740
At this point, the moon's gravity has a stronger pull on their capsule than Earth's.

11090
12:14:54,220 --> 12:14:58,020
They will lose communications for about 40 minutes while passing behind the moon,

11091
12:14:58,300 --> 12:15:01,460
where they are also expected to witness a solar eclipse.

11092
12:15:03,570 --> 12:15:07,130
Our coverage of the war between the U.S., Israel and Iran continues

11093
12:15:07,130 --> 12:15:09,810
after the listening post. Stay with Al Jazeera.

11094
12:15:10,930 --> 12:15:15,850
The United States military began major combat operations in Iran.

11095
12:15:16,010 --> 12:15:20,770
We are not joined by the U.S. and Israeli offensive scruples.

11096
12:15:22,410 --> 12:15:25,610
The position of the Spanish government can be summed up in four words.

11097
12:15:25,890 --> 12:15:26,930
No to the war.

11098
12:15:27,170 --> 12:15:31,850
I have condemned the massive military strikes by the United States and Israel.

11099
12:15:31,970 --> 12:15:35,090
And I also condemn the subsequent attacks by Iran.

11100
12:15:35,090 --> 12:15:38,890
The attacks on energy capacity that has happened on both sides

11101
12:15:39,010 --> 12:15:42,090
is a dangerous precedent that will cause repercussions throughout the world.

11102
12:15:42,170 --> 12:15:46,490
We can now see a regional conflict with unintended consequences.

11103
12:15:46,810 --> 12:15:50,290
Stay with us for the latest developments on Al Jazeera.

11104
12:15:51,520 --> 12:15:54,320
President Trump launched the war in Iran a month ago,

11105
12:15:54,560 --> 12:15:55,800
but does he know how to end it?

11106
12:15:56,600 --> 12:15:59,800
Now European leaders say they'll help Trump on the Strait of Hormuz,

11107
12:15:59,800 --> 12:16:02,880
but how much damage will be done to U.S.-European relations

11108
12:16:03,120 --> 12:16:06,480
long after Trump's epic fury subsides?

11109
12:16:06,680 --> 12:16:10,200
Your weekly take on U.S. politics, the bottom line.

11110
12:16:10,840 --> 12:16:13,560
This week, our coverage of the war on Iran

11111
12:16:13,560 --> 12:16:16,280
starts with the media story coming out of Israel.

11112
12:16:16,680 --> 12:16:19,400
Citizens there are not getting the full picture.

11113
12:16:19,680 --> 12:16:22,520
Military censors are filtering what they see.

11114
12:16:22,960 --> 12:16:24,760
Israel is growing more oppressive,

11115
12:16:25,000 --> 12:16:28,520
whether it's free speech or a new law that could sentence Palestinians

11116
12:16:28,720 --> 12:16:34,200
to death by execution, translating propaganda and exporting it online.

11117
12:16:34,480 --> 12:16:37,240
Israel in Persian is the name of the account

11118
12:16:37,520 --> 12:16:42,440
and it's being used to target Iranians, plus the Iranian countermeasures.

11119
12:16:42,680 --> 12:16:44,880
They include an internet blackout.

11120
12:16:45,000 --> 12:16:48,640
This is a way for them to show the populace that they are in control

11121
12:16:48,840 --> 12:16:54,720
and exporting their own content, including AI in the battle over hearts and minds.

11122
12:17:01,560 --> 12:17:07,320
The fog of war created by the U.S.-Israeli attack on Iran is not lifting, it is thickening.

11123
12:17:07,720 --> 12:17:11,720
Mixed messages keep coming out of Washington, rehashed by the day,

11124
12:17:11,720 --> 12:17:14,800
it seems, generating more confusion than clarity.

11125
12:17:15,080 --> 12:17:17,760
In Israel, the gap between political rhetoric

11126
12:17:17,960 --> 12:17:20,480
and the on-the-ground reality has been widening.

11127
12:17:20,840 --> 12:17:23,600
The Netanyahu government's prediction of a quick war

11128
12:17:23,880 --> 12:17:27,520
to topple Iran's leadership and destroy its nuclear program

11129
12:17:27,720 --> 12:17:30,560
has given way to a reality that is far messier

11130
12:17:30,760 --> 12:17:33,680
and much more dangerous for Israeli civilians.

11131
12:17:34,120 --> 12:17:38,920
Complicating matters further still is what Israelis are allowed to see of this war.

11132
12:17:39,160 --> 12:17:41,400
That is being tightly controlled.

11133
12:17:41,800 --> 12:17:45,640
Journalists face unprecedented levels of military censorship

11134
12:17:45,920 --> 12:17:50,520
while being urged to raise morale rather than just report the facts.

11135
12:17:50,880 --> 12:17:53,720
And Israelis who do push back against the war

11136
12:17:53,880 --> 12:17:57,720
or against a controversial new law legalizing the death penalty

11137
12:17:57,920 --> 12:18:02,760
but only against Palestinians know that the authorities are out to repress them,

11138
12:18:03,080 --> 12:18:06,700
if not silenced.

11139
12:18:06,700 --> 12:18:09,300
Benjamin Netanyahu wouldn't put it this way,

11140
12:18:09,380 --> 12:18:12,860
but five weeks into the U.S.-Israeli war against Iran,

11141
12:18:13,060 --> 12:18:15,580
this is what he's up against domestically.

11142
12:18:16,060 --> 12:18:18,980
Iranian missiles keep hitting Israeli targets,

11143
12:18:19,260 --> 12:18:23,220
causing casualties and severely injuring the country's infrastructure.

11144
12:18:23,780 --> 12:18:27,300
The collapse that Israel was hoping for of the Iranian government,

11145
12:18:27,580 --> 12:18:30,860
the galvanizing of rebellion there, has not happened.

11146
12:18:31,420 --> 12:18:34,020
Given the multiple fronts and entanglements,

11147
12:18:34,100 --> 12:18:36,420
Lebanon, the West Bank, Gaza,

11148
12:18:36,620 --> 12:18:39,900
and the unprecedented number of reservists called up,

11149
12:18:40,180 --> 12:18:42,620
Israel risks running out of soldiers.

11150
12:18:42,940 --> 12:18:45,260
And like his ally, Donald Trump,

11151
12:18:45,460 --> 12:18:48,100
Netanyahu has no clear exit strategy.

11152
12:18:49,140 --> 12:18:52,380
What he can be countered on, however, at times like these,

11153
12:18:52,540 --> 12:18:56,340
is having a media strategy, scapegoating his crates.

11154
12:19:04,500 --> 12:19:08,020
In the theatrics that Netanyahu sometimes indulges in,

11155
12:19:08,180 --> 12:19:10,780
he says, what are you doing in the TV studios?

11156
12:19:11,420 --> 12:19:15,260
Why are you sapping the morale of the public?

11157
12:19:15,460 --> 12:19:19,140
Why are you helping the enemy, not our own people?

11158
12:19:20,140 --> 12:19:25,420
And that's Netanyahu calling out the media for two and a half years.

11159
12:19:25,620 --> 12:19:28,140
You've done the job designated to you

11160
12:19:28,340 --> 12:19:33,620
of being a fully mobilized machine to create consensus for genocide.

11161
12:19:33,820 --> 12:19:36,300
And now to make sure this war can continue indefinitely.

11162
12:19:36,500 --> 12:19:38,940
And those are your marching orders and go back to them.

11163
12:19:39,740 --> 12:19:42,570
Those orders in their most specific form

11164
12:19:42,770 --> 12:19:44,970
come from Israel's military censors.

11165
12:19:44,970 --> 12:19:48,090
In the war, we're Israelis, before we're refugees, right?

11166
12:19:48,290 --> 12:19:51,370
But what happens when refugees come to the censor?

11167
12:19:51,570 --> 12:19:52,970
He says, no, no.

11168
12:20:00,000 --> 12:20:02,760
whether the country is at war or not.

11169
12:20:02,760 --> 12:20:08,060
But reporters and citizens alike say they have never seen censorship to this extent, where

11170
12:20:08,060 --> 12:20:14,530
it can inadvertently put the citizens the censors are supposed to protect at greater risk.

11171
12:20:14,530 --> 12:20:18,910
Nader Gontar's works for the Israeli newspaper Haaretz.

11172
12:20:18,910 --> 12:20:23,750
After a military base was hit by an Iranian missile, he went on X, saying, it's nice

11173
12:20:23,750 --> 12:20:28,310
that they put up warning signs about the asbestos, scattered from the military base

11174
12:20:28,310 --> 12:20:31,150
throughout the neighborhood following the strike.

11175
12:20:31,150 --> 12:20:36,310
But no government official explained what the implications and dangers are, what the kids

11176
12:20:36,310 --> 12:20:42,870
are breathing, while the soldiers on the base walk around in protective suits and masks.

11177
12:20:42,870 --> 12:20:48,630
Tightly controlled images and carefully shaped narratives from Israel, AI material on social

11178
12:20:48,630 --> 12:20:52,830
media designed to exaggerate Iran's military prowess.

11179
12:20:52,830 --> 12:20:58,670
Combined with videos first posted weeks ago of missile strikes on Israeli targets, then

11180
12:20:58,670 --> 12:21:03,950
reposted and presented as new, have caused all kinds of confusion.

11181
12:21:03,950 --> 12:21:09,030
With mainstream outlets under the thumb of the censors, Israelis are scouring sources

11182
12:21:09,030 --> 12:21:15,310
online where it is increasingly difficult to separate fact from fiction, reality from

11183
12:21:15,310 --> 12:21:17,200
propaganda.

11184
12:21:17,200 --> 12:21:22,300
The image that you see out of Israel is very carefully choreographed.

11185
12:21:22,300 --> 12:21:28,660
This is a country self-professed as a democracy, but it has a military sensor that can and

11186
12:21:28,660 --> 12:21:35,780
does control the kind of information that can be used or disseminated by the media.

11187
12:21:35,780 --> 12:21:42,100
But in this war, the kind of restrictions that have been imposed are unprecedented.

11188
12:21:42,100 --> 12:21:46,760
The only thing you see are damage to civilian areas and so on.

11189
12:21:46,760 --> 12:21:51,180
You know that you're not getting the full picture and that in itself tells you that

11190
12:21:51,180 --> 12:21:54,260
it's something that the state doesn't want you to know about.

11191
12:21:54,260 --> 12:22:02,260
They are definitely trying to portray an Israel that is much more capable of defending itself

11192
12:22:02,260 --> 12:22:09,580
than it actually is and is implying that Iran knows less about the country's infrastructure

11193
12:22:09,580 --> 12:22:12,140
and sensitive sites than it does.

11194
12:22:12,140 --> 12:22:18,550
There is a reason why only after the fact when Israeli officials are on the scene

11195
12:22:18,550 --> 12:22:24,670
are news crews able to film exact locations of strike sites and why most of these videos

11196
12:22:24,670 --> 12:22:29,990
of sensitive sites being bombed are oftentimes by anonymous people, not journalists on the

11197
12:22:29,990 --> 12:22:31,470
ground.

11198
12:22:31,470 --> 12:22:37,470
Although the percentage has fallen slightly from roughly 90% down to 80, an overwhelming

11199
12:22:37,470 --> 12:22:41,310
majority of Jewish Israelis still support this war.

11200
12:22:41,310 --> 12:22:45,870
The authorities are out to keep it that way, cracking down on the relatively small

11201
12:22:45,870 --> 12:22:48,590
anti-war protests on the streets.

11202
12:22:48,590 --> 12:22:56,470
This protest says she was roughed up just for being there.

11203
12:22:56,470 --> 12:23:01,190
Another demonstration called after Israel's parliament passed a new capital punishment

11204
12:23:01,190 --> 12:23:06,030
law applicable only to Palestinians got similar treatment.

11205
12:23:06,030 --> 12:23:09,790
Protesters rounded up, journalists hit by water cannons.

11206
12:23:09,790 --> 12:23:15,150
For the security minister who championed the law, Itamar Ben Gavir, its passage was

11207
12:23:15,150 --> 12:23:19,650
a champagne moment worth savoring.

11208
12:23:19,650 --> 12:23:25,730
For this popular and sometimes depraved Israeli TV comedy show, the prospect of executing

11209
12:23:25,730 --> 12:23:28,970
Palestinians was played for laughs.

11210
12:23:28,970 --> 12:23:32,450
So what did you start to do to protect the human form, let's say, because my name is

11211
12:23:32,450 --> 12:23:35,050
also a massage?

11212
12:23:35,050 --> 12:23:41,850
The law essentially forces the death penalty on Palestinian prisoners who are convicted

11213
12:23:41,850 --> 12:23:43,930
of terrorism offenses.

11214
12:23:43,930 --> 12:23:48,890
But even within opposition to this law, it was on the basis that it would threaten

11215
12:23:48,890 --> 12:23:56,050
potential future Israeli hostages, not the crime of mass executing by hanging Palestinian

11216
12:23:56,050 --> 12:23:57,410
detainees.

11217
12:23:57,410 --> 12:24:03,010
So it's a problem of process, not of moral depravity.

11218
12:24:03,010 --> 12:24:06,890
And this was an extremely popular bill amongst the Israeli public.

11219
12:24:06,890 --> 12:24:15,010
I went to the protest in Tel Aviv and the security forces were very quick to crack

11220
12:24:15,010 --> 12:24:16,010
down.

11221
12:24:16,010 --> 12:24:17,010
I'm a journalist.

11222
12:24:17,010 --> 12:24:21,080
I'm filming and they took a clearly aggressive position.

11223
12:24:21,080 --> 12:24:22,080
The death penalty.

11224
12:24:22,080 --> 12:24:25,160
Some people say, well, there will be challenges that will never really be implemented even

11225
12:24:25,160 --> 12:24:26,160
if it is passed.

11226
12:24:26,160 --> 12:24:27,640
I don't think it matters.

11227
12:24:27,640 --> 12:24:32,380
These are signposts of where a country is going and it is not a good direction.

11228
12:24:32,380 --> 12:24:37,560
With news feeds still dominated by Iran's blocking of the Strait of Hormuz, the Israeli

11229
12:24:37,560 --> 12:24:43,820
occupation of south Lebanon, the missiles still landing in Israel and Iran, the typically

11230
12:24:43,820 --> 12:24:49,660
scant coverage of Israeli settler violence in the West Bank has all but evaporated.

11231
12:24:49,660 --> 12:24:54,940
When the West Bank story does get reported in Israel, the settlers are usually described

11232
12:24:54,940 --> 12:25:06,100
as rogue operators separate from the state and the army that supports them.

11233
12:25:06,100 --> 12:25:11,500
This week, an American news crew from CNN was confronted by Israeli soldiers in the

11234
12:25:11,500 --> 12:25:17,660
West Bank, their guns pointed at the journalists, one of whom was put in a chokehold.

11235
12:25:17,660 --> 12:25:23,260
That story made news even in Israel, not because it happened, but because of who it

11236
12:25:23,260 --> 12:25:24,260
happened to.

11237
12:25:24,260 --> 12:25:30,180
It's rare to hear these soldiers speak so openly, especially to foreign media.

11238
12:25:30,180 --> 12:25:35,300
They believe that all of the West Bank is Israel's land, that it is Jewish territory

11239
12:25:35,300 --> 12:25:36,300
only.

11240
12:25:36,300 --> 12:25:43,380
I watched that report from our colleagues at CNN and I would never dare do what he did

11241
12:25:43,380 --> 12:25:48,740
because had this crew not been an American crew, things would have turned out very different.

11242
12:25:48,740 --> 12:25:53,860
Many of our colleagues were beaten to a pulp in similar situations because they were

11243
12:25:53,860 --> 12:25:55,360
Palestinian.

11244
12:25:55,360 --> 12:26:01,060
But Israelis don't hear and don't see what happens to Palestinians in the occupied

11245
12:26:01,060 --> 12:26:02,580
West Bank.

11246
12:26:02,580 --> 12:26:05,880
And at this point, most of them don't care.

11247
12:26:05,880 --> 12:26:11,720
They want to try to show that they are doing something about Israeli perpetrators committing

11248
12:26:11,720 --> 12:26:15,680
terrorist attacks in the West Bank, to show the White House primarily that they're doing

11249
12:26:15,680 --> 12:26:16,680
something.

11250
12:26:16,680 --> 12:26:20,600
But it's really the system of settlement expansion, annexation.

11251
12:26:20,600 --> 12:26:22,720
Many Israelis will say, oh yes, it's terrible.

11252
12:26:22,720 --> 12:26:35,480
These very few people, a handful of bad eggs.

11253
12:26:35,480 --> 12:26:38,600
And what the settler leaders say is that many of them are not even from the settlements,

11254
12:26:38,600 --> 12:26:41,920
they're troubled youth, that they give the entire settlement project a bad name.

11255
12:26:41,920 --> 12:26:45,640
We better crack down on them so that we can continue expanding the settlement project.

11256
12:26:45,640 --> 12:26:47,640
That's what they say very openly.

11257
12:26:47,640 --> 12:26:57,400
Israel is in an impunity-fuelled march towards seeing how far it can go to impose

11258
12:26:57,400 --> 12:27:04,600
its domination, the largest military operations in the West Bank in half a century, seizing

11259
12:27:04,600 --> 12:27:09,320
more territory in Lebanon, still holding 60% of Gaza.

11260
12:27:09,320 --> 12:27:12,320
That continues as long as Israel can get away with it.

11261
12:27:12,320 --> 12:27:18,190
But it only actually becomes overreach when blowback arrives.

11262
12:27:18,190 --> 12:27:25,300
When something holds Israel to account diplomatically or on the battlefield.

11263
12:27:25,300 --> 12:27:34,440
And unless that moment comes, I don't expect the Israeli side to recognize how far out

11264
12:27:34,440 --> 12:27:40,380
of its depth this may take it.

11265
12:27:40,380 --> 12:27:46,220
Staying with Israel and the propaganda it has directed at Iranians in their native tongue.

11266
12:27:46,220 --> 12:27:51,800
This is a playbook we've seen before with Palestinians, Tarek Nafa is here with more.

11267
12:27:51,800 --> 12:27:56,600
Since the start of the war on Iran, one of the most active platforms for messaging

11268
12:27:56,600 --> 12:28:02,840
aimed at Iranians has been Israel in Persian, the Israeli government's official Farsi

11269
12:28:02,840 --> 12:28:05,240
language account on X.

11270
12:28:05,240 --> 12:28:11,280
It's posted a steady stream of content mocking Iran's leaders, framing them as the drivers

11271
12:28:11,280 --> 12:28:16,920
of this conflict and trying to position Israel as a friend of Iranians.

11272
12:28:16,920 --> 12:28:21,680
This week the account posted this video ridiculing a woman whose home had just been

11273
12:28:21,680 --> 12:28:27,280
destroyed in an airstrike because she was holding a nice handbag.

11274
12:28:27,280 --> 12:28:32,400
There are also these posts which suggested scenes of destruction in Tehran had been

11275
12:28:32,400 --> 12:28:36,960
fabricated by the Iranian government using a paid actor.

11276
12:28:36,960 --> 12:28:41,040
These claims have been thoroughly debunked by fact checkers, but that hasn't stopped

11277
12:28:41,040 --> 12:28:46,840
this narrative that the Iranians are faking it from spreading, including by voices in

11278
12:28:46,840 --> 12:28:52,260
the Iranian diaspora who are supportive of the Israeli-U.S. war.

11279
12:28:52,260 --> 12:28:56,460
Casting doubt on victims questioning their legitimacy, these are tactics that the

11280
12:28:56,460 --> 12:29:02,220
Israelis have used before on Palestinians, summed up in terms like Pollywood that

11281
12:29:02,220 --> 12:29:05,660
suggests Palestinians have staged their own suffering.

11282
12:29:05,660 --> 12:29:11,860
Another Farsi language account is operated by Mossad, Israel's Foreign Intelligence Agency.

11283
12:29:11,860 --> 12:29:17,050
It is being used to openly try and recruit Iranians as spies.

11284
12:29:17,050 --> 12:29:21,810
Just as it has done elsewhere in the region in Arabic, Israel's use of Farsi

11285
12:29:21,810 --> 12:29:27,650
is designed to whitewash its image and shape public opinion, leaving Iranians with the

11286
12:29:27,650 --> 12:29:32,370
realization that even their online spaces have been infiltrated.

11287
12:29:32,370 --> 12:29:34,410
Thanks Tarek.

11288
12:29:34,410 --> 12:29:38,330
Turning now to the counter-narrative, the one that's coming out of Tehran.

11289
12:29:38,330 --> 12:29:42,450
Officials there have been framing their case to international audiences, tailoring their

11290
12:29:42,450 --> 12:29:47,650
language and ideas accordingly while accusing Western media outlets of distorting the

11291
12:29:47,650 --> 12:29:49,570
facts of this war.

11292
12:29:49,570 --> 12:29:54,810
Inside Iran, a sweeping internet blackout remains in place severely limiting what people

11293
12:29:54,810 --> 12:29:56,770
can see and share.

11294
12:29:56,770 --> 12:30:03,010
And a new front has been opened, shaped by some increasingly sophisticated AI content, further

11295
12:30:03,010 --> 12:30:06,890
blurring the line between information and the truth.

11296
12:30:06,890 --> 12:30:11,290
To help us understand the strategy behind all of this, we're joined now from Washington

11297
12:30:11,290 --> 12:30:16,490
by the Executive Vice President of the Quincy Institute for Responsible Statecraft,

11298
12:30:16,490 --> 12:30:17,490
Trita Parsi.

11299
12:30:17,730 --> 12:30:19,610
Mr. Parsi, let's start with this.

11300
12:30:19,610 --> 12:30:25,490
This past week, Iran's President, Masoud Pazeshkian, addressed an open letter to the American people,

11301
12:30:25,490 --> 12:30:31,210
urging them to look beyond what he called a machinery of misinformation in the US.

11302
12:30:31,210 --> 12:30:35,850
What are the chances of a message like that actually cutting through, given the current

11303
12:30:35,850 --> 12:30:39,480
media environment in America?

11304
12:30:39,480 --> 12:30:44,480
I find the likelihood of that message getting through to be rather limited.

11305
12:30:44,480 --> 12:30:48,960
At the end of the day, the American public is very skeptical of this war.

11306
12:30:48,960 --> 12:30:53,920
Even Trump's voters are starting to turn against this war, and certainly they're already very

11307
12:30:53,920 --> 12:30:56,680
much against going in with ground troops.

11308
12:30:56,680 --> 12:31:02,440
But the Iranian government's ability to be able to take advantage of some of those schisms

11309
12:31:02,440 --> 12:31:08,800
beyond scoring points on social media, I've not seen any clear signs that there is

11310
12:31:08,800 --> 12:31:09,800
any success there.

11311
12:31:09,800 --> 12:31:16,080
And again, through the mainstream media, you will hardly be able to get any impact from

11312
12:31:16,080 --> 12:31:17,080
that end.

11313
12:31:17,080 --> 12:31:21,400
But the Iranians are nevertheless doing this because from their standpoint, this is not

11314
12:31:21,400 --> 12:31:22,400
America's war.

11315
12:31:22,400 --> 12:31:26,760
They strongly believe that Israel led America into this war.

11316
12:31:26,760 --> 12:31:30,200
And the more they can hammer that point home with an American audience that already

11317
12:31:30,200 --> 12:31:35,040
is very receptive to that view, particularly on the right, the more they think they

11318
12:31:35,040 --> 12:31:39,880
can increase the opposition inside of the US against this war.

11319
12:31:39,880 --> 12:31:44,720
Now the Iranian state is displaying some online skills here that many in the West were

11320
12:31:44,720 --> 12:31:49,080
unaware that it had, both the foreign minister and the Speaker of the Parliament there have

11321
12:31:49,080 --> 12:32:07,240
acquired a fan following on X, and there are AI animations that are in the mix as well.

11322
12:32:07,240 --> 12:32:09,600
What are the core messages being sent here?

11323
12:32:09,600 --> 12:32:16,120
How effective do you think those techniques have been in influencing public opinion outside

11324
12:32:16,120 --> 12:32:18,930
of Iran?

11325
12:32:18,930 --> 12:32:23,530
It's really fascinating because I don't know if there's been a lot of other major wars that

11326
12:32:23,530 --> 12:32:33,530
simultaneously have been fought on the ground, but also within an arena of meme wars, essentially.

11327
12:32:33,530 --> 12:32:39,850
Various videos produced by both sides, propaganda videos, AI produced propaganda videos.

11328
12:32:39,850 --> 12:32:42,610
We really haven't seen that until this war.

11329
12:32:42,610 --> 12:32:45,170
And the Iranians are clearly scoring some points.

11330
12:32:45,410 --> 12:32:52,010
Whether that is the core reason why the public is negative to this war or not is really difficult

11331
12:32:52,010 --> 12:32:57,250
to disaggregate, because at the end of the day, the public was overwhelmingly against

11332
12:32:57,250 --> 12:32:59,050
this war from the outset.

11333
12:32:59,050 --> 12:33:02,490
It may have reinforced their opposition to it.

11334
12:33:02,490 --> 12:33:07,770
It may have made it stronger, but I don't think it necessarily has led to a shift in

11335
12:33:07,770 --> 12:33:08,770
public opinion.

11336
12:33:08,770 --> 12:33:13,730
If anything, what has shifted is because of higher gas prices, a clear sign that

11337
12:33:13,770 --> 12:33:15,850
Trump doesn't have a plan.

11338
12:33:15,850 --> 12:33:19,890
And certainly, I think there will be an even greater shift if he goes in with ground troops

11339
12:33:19,890 --> 12:33:24,570
and you have a large number of American soldiers coming home in coffins.

11340
12:33:24,570 --> 12:33:28,010
Let's turn to Iran itself now, the internal narrative there.

11341
12:33:28,010 --> 12:33:31,650
The Iranian authorities, as you know, have largely blacked out the internet there for

11342
12:33:31,650 --> 12:33:33,330
more than a month now.

11343
12:33:33,330 --> 12:33:35,130
And it's not the first time that this has happened.

11344
12:33:35,130 --> 12:33:41,570
Give us an idea of how crippled communications are there with the outside world.

11345
12:33:41,570 --> 12:33:49,770
What is this blackout and the censorship within the Iranian media space defensible in your view?

11346
12:33:49,770 --> 12:33:58,210
So the manner in which the government closed the internet entirely on January 8th, roughly

11347
12:33:58,210 --> 12:34:03,610
till January 10th, and then slowly, slowly they'd open it up, is a degree of closure

11348
12:34:03,610 --> 12:34:05,970
I don't think we have ever seen before.

11349
12:34:05,970 --> 12:34:10,770
And it's during this short period as well that a very large number of Iranian protesters

11350
12:34:10,850 --> 12:34:15,610
and others were killed by the government, but also by some elements

11351
12:34:15,610 --> 12:34:18,870
amongst the protesters who used violence.

11352
12:34:18,870 --> 12:34:22,230
That level of closure is not what you're having right now.

11353
12:34:22,230 --> 12:34:24,430
There's still a lot of limitations.

11354
12:34:24,430 --> 12:34:27,990
It's still difficult to get through to friends, etc.

11355
12:34:27,990 --> 12:34:30,870
But if they use VPNs, etc., it is possible.

11356
12:34:30,870 --> 12:34:35,710
Whereas during those first couple of days in January, even with VPNs,

11357
12:34:35,710 --> 12:34:38,870
even with Starlink, it was very difficult to get in touch with people

11358
12:34:38,870 --> 12:34:43,860
because the Iranian government was shutting everything down and jamming Starlink as well.

11359
12:34:43,860 --> 12:34:48,820
What do you make of the Iranian authorities and their argument that part of this is defensive,

11360
12:34:48,820 --> 12:34:54,700
protecting Iranians and their institutions by blocking off the outside world

11361
12:34:54,700 --> 12:34:58,310
from penetrating via the internet?

11362
12:34:58,310 --> 12:35:01,990
Well, let's first remind ourselves that during these times of war,

11363
12:35:01,990 --> 12:35:06,110
this is measures not necessarily similar to this one,

11364
12:35:06,110 --> 12:35:08,390
but others that are taken by almost everyone.

11365
12:35:08,390 --> 12:35:13,990
So in Israel right now, if you film Iranian missiles hitting Israel, you can end up in jail.

11366
12:35:13,990 --> 12:35:18,030
Same thing is happening in Dubai in which everything is being censored right now

11367
12:35:18,030 --> 12:35:21,470
in order to make sure that this information does not come out.

11368
12:35:21,470 --> 12:35:25,390
Now, internal communication has not been blocked by those countries.

11369
12:35:25,390 --> 12:35:27,870
It has been by the Iranian government.

11370
12:35:27,870 --> 12:35:32,910
Now, is there an element of truth in some of what they're saying?

11371
12:35:32,910 --> 12:35:38,590
I think there is because you already have admissions from the former head of the CIA

11372
12:35:38,590 --> 12:35:45,310
that Mossad and other American agents were on the ground in Iran during those days of protests.

11373
12:35:45,310 --> 12:35:49,830
You have opposition figures who have more or less admitted

11374
12:35:49,830 --> 12:35:56,440
that there were some of their elements that also stood for some of the violence.

11375
12:35:56,440 --> 12:36:00,000
But is that the only reason why the government is shutting it down?

11376
12:36:00,000 --> 12:36:04,640
No, I think this is both because of those first stated reasons,

11377
12:36:04,640 --> 12:36:09,360
but also because this is a way for them to show the populace that they are in control

11378
12:36:09,360 --> 12:36:13,360
and that they will tolerate absolutely no uprisings or protests,

11379
12:36:13,360 --> 12:36:17,440
but also in order to make sure that outside elements that are trying to penetrate Iran

11380
12:36:17,440 --> 12:36:20,000
during these sensitive times are blocked.

11381
12:36:20,000 --> 12:36:25,000
What do you make of the IRGC, the Iranian Revolutionary Guard Corps message

11382
12:36:25,000 --> 12:36:29,360
from just a few days back that it would target all those U.S. tech companies,

11383
12:36:29,360 --> 12:36:34,240
including Apple, Google, Metta, Amazon and Palantir?

11384
12:36:34,280 --> 12:36:41,840
And what does that list of targets tell you about Iran's larger strategy in this war?

11385
12:36:41,840 --> 12:36:49,320
Well, the larger strategy is that they're going after elements that exist within the GCC countries

11386
12:36:49,320 --> 12:36:53,360
that are being used directly or indirectly by the United States

11387
12:36:53,360 --> 12:36:56,880
in order to conduct the offensive elements of this war.

