12084
13:25:16,180 --> 13:25:19,940
as opposed to the elders that have all been killed?

12085
13:25:19,940 --> 13:25:22,460
But in one word, it is not as experienced

12086
13:25:22,460 --> 13:25:24,100
as the previous ones.

12087
13:25:24,100 --> 13:25:26,580
This is leadership which has come on board,

12088
13:25:26,580 --> 13:25:28,260
especially if you look at the military leaders

12089
13:25:28,260 --> 13:25:30,340
that have come to the front,

12090
13:25:30,340 --> 13:25:35,340
are younger, are not as known in the battlefields

12091
13:25:35,380 --> 13:25:38,020
as the previous ones who had fought wars.

12092
13:25:38,020 --> 13:25:40,460
So essentially what the Pakistanis are dealing with

12093
13:25:40,460 --> 13:25:43,180
are people who, A, feel that they have

12094
13:25:43,180 --> 13:25:44,780
the upper hand militarily,

12095
13:25:44,780 --> 13:25:48,140
B, want to tell their people what are they made of,

12096
13:25:48,140 --> 13:25:51,380
what they can teach the enemy in a battle space.

12097
13:25:51,380 --> 13:25:53,780
But building on to what Mohammad just said,

12098
13:25:54,860 --> 13:25:59,020
there is multiple off-ramps that are still available.

12099
13:25:59,020 --> 13:26:01,660
I asked some sources about this question of,

12100
13:26:01,660 --> 13:26:02,500
what gives you hope?

12101
13:26:02,500 --> 13:26:04,460
Because these are maximalist positions,

12102
13:26:04,460 --> 13:26:05,620
nobody's willing to budge.

12103
13:26:05,620 --> 13:26:06,820
And what I was told,

12104
13:26:06,820 --> 13:26:09,100
that while you'll see a lot of chest thumping

12105
13:26:09,100 --> 13:26:12,300
on the airways, there is quiet diplomacy taking place.

12106
13:26:12,300 --> 13:26:14,100
And indication was the deadline.

12107
13:26:14,100 --> 13:26:16,620
It wasn't this deadline that was extended by Donald Trump.

12108
13:26:16,620 --> 13:26:17,460
It was the previous one.

12109
13:26:17,460 --> 13:26:20,820
It was two days, then it was a week, then it was 10 days.

12110
13:26:20,820 --> 13:26:22,260
And now another day extension.

12111
13:26:22,260 --> 13:26:24,140
So do you think we could see an extension to this one?

12112
13:26:24,140 --> 13:26:27,140
People who are involved in this believe

12113
13:26:27,140 --> 13:26:29,380
that there might be another extension to this

12114
13:26:29,380 --> 13:26:31,940
because of the sheer inability of people

12115
13:26:31,940 --> 13:26:33,300
to communicate within Iran,

12116
13:26:33,300 --> 13:26:35,420
because so much of the infrastructure

12117
13:26:35,420 --> 13:26:38,340
as well as command structure has been degraded.

12118
13:26:38,340 --> 13:26:40,420
And that is why you're seeing diplomacy

12119
13:26:40,420 --> 13:26:42,620
when it comes to Iranian stalking to the French,

12120
13:26:42,660 --> 13:26:45,740
Iranians stalking to diplomats of the region.

12121
13:26:45,740 --> 13:26:49,580
And frantic phone calls between Ankara, Riyadh,

12122
13:26:49,580 --> 13:26:52,020
you're seeing them in Oman,

12123
13:26:52,020 --> 13:26:55,020
speaking to them about a possibility of an opening.

12124
13:26:55,020 --> 13:26:57,100
Just before coming here, I was talking to somebody

12125
13:26:57,100 --> 13:26:58,300
and they said that, look,

12126
13:26:58,300 --> 13:27:01,500
if the Iranians wanted to tell the Americans a message,

12127
13:27:01,500 --> 13:27:04,300
they've let 15 ships go through the Strait of Omuz

12128
13:27:04,300 --> 13:27:05,380
in the last 24 hours.

12129
13:27:05,380 --> 13:27:07,300
So there is a partial reopening

12130
13:27:07,300 --> 13:27:09,580
if the American president wanted to sell it as that.

12131
13:27:09,580 --> 13:27:10,980
So there are multiple avenues

12132
13:27:10,980 --> 13:27:14,020
if there is serious impetus behind finding peace.

12133
13:27:14,020 --> 13:27:16,660
But as Mohammed said, the real equation,

12134
13:27:16,660 --> 13:27:18,980
the real deal breaker here is Israel,

12135
13:27:18,980 --> 13:27:20,580
as you've seen time and again,

12136
13:27:20,580 --> 13:27:22,860
even diplomats who were involved in this

12137
13:27:22,860 --> 13:27:24,540
have been targeted.

12138
13:27:24,540 --> 13:27:28,660
Michael, to you, one last question, Michael Shubrid.

12139
13:27:28,660 --> 13:27:30,580
Just 15 minutes ago, I thought perhaps

12140
13:27:30,580 --> 13:27:31,940
based on what Trump was saying

12141
13:27:31,940 --> 13:27:34,660
is that there could be negotiations

12142
13:27:34,660 --> 13:27:37,780
to sort of end this idea of Israel

12143
13:27:37,780 --> 13:27:39,860
and the U.S. pummeling Iran

12144
13:27:39,860 --> 13:27:41,180
and its infrastructure.

12145
13:27:41,180 --> 13:27:42,940
But now hearing from Osama

12146
13:27:42,940 --> 13:27:46,020
and also hearing from the spokesman for the Iranian farmers,

12147
13:27:46,020 --> 13:27:48,100
it seems Iran is intent

12148
13:27:48,100 --> 13:27:49,780
that they are feeling more emboldened

12149
13:27:49,780 --> 13:27:52,940
and they intend to get what they want out of this.

12150
13:27:52,940 --> 13:27:57,180
So Trump really is in a sort of difficult position also

12151
13:27:57,180 --> 13:28:00,420
because whatever the U.S. decides to do next,

12152
13:28:00,420 --> 13:28:03,060
the repercussions will be felt in the region here,

12153
13:28:03,060 --> 13:28:03,980
in the GCC.

12154
13:28:03,980 --> 13:28:05,740
If it's been an eye for an eye,

12155
13:28:05,740 --> 13:28:07,260
it's tipped for tact throughout this whole war

12156
13:28:07,260 --> 13:28:09,060
and Iran won't hold back, it said.

12157
13:28:11,310 --> 13:28:12,190
Well, exactly.

12158
13:28:12,190 --> 13:28:16,510
So the problem here is that Donald Trump

12159
13:28:16,510 --> 13:28:20,670
has to make some gesture to the Iranians

12160
13:28:20,670 --> 13:28:24,670
and it's hard for that not to look like him backing down.

12161
13:28:24,670 --> 13:28:28,670
So my concern is that's not what's going

12162
13:28:28,670 --> 13:28:31,310
through the American president's mind.

12163
13:28:31,310 --> 13:28:34,510
What he wants to do is double down

12164
13:28:34,510 --> 13:28:36,630
and cause more damage

12165
13:28:36,630 --> 13:28:40,310
to look like he's in the position of strength

12166
13:28:40,310 --> 13:28:43,990
and I hope that he's getting enough advice

12167
13:28:43,990 --> 13:28:46,350
about the broader damage to the region

12168
13:28:46,350 --> 13:28:48,710
that that would likely provoke

12169
13:28:48,710 --> 13:28:52,230
and about the damage to the global economy from that.

12170
13:28:52,230 --> 13:28:55,750
That to me, that sort of fear of the markets,

12171
13:28:55,750 --> 13:28:58,270
fear of gasoline prices,

12172
13:28:58,270 --> 13:29:02,030
that's more likely to be the thing that moderates him

12173
13:29:02,030 --> 13:29:06,190
but I think the risks of broad escalation

12174
13:29:06,190 --> 13:29:09,150
happening soon are very high.

12175
13:29:09,150 --> 13:29:09,990
All right, thank you.

12176
13:29:09,990 --> 13:29:11,510
I'd like to thank all of you.

12177
13:29:11,510 --> 13:29:13,870
Michael and Shoebridge in Australia.

12178
13:29:13,870 --> 13:29:16,830
We also had Mohammed Mastri here in the studio

12179
13:29:16,830 --> 13:29:19,350
as well as Salman bin Javed, our senior correspondent.

12180
13:29:19,350 --> 13:29:20,990
Thank you very much, gentlemen.

12181
13:29:20,990 --> 13:29:22,550
Right, well, US president Donald Trump

12182
13:29:22,550 --> 13:29:25,030
has been giving Iran shifting deadlines

12183
13:29:25,030 --> 13:29:26,710
to reopen the Strait of Hormuz

12184
13:29:26,710 --> 13:29:29,430
and that says Iran insists the key waterway

12185
13:29:29,430 --> 13:29:31,670
isn't actually closed and that only ships

12186
13:29:31,670 --> 13:29:34,670
that belong to its enemies are barred from passage.

12187
13:29:34,670 --> 13:29:38,150
Trump issued his first ultimatum on March 21st.

12188
13:29:38,150 --> 13:29:40,350
He threatened to bomb Iran's power plants

12189
13:29:40,350 --> 13:29:43,310
if the Strait wasn't reopened within 48 hours

12190
13:29:43,310 --> 13:29:46,230
and he later extended that deadline by five days

12191
13:29:46,230 --> 13:29:49,350
claiming that negotiations were underway.

12192
13:29:49,350 --> 13:29:52,870
Trump issued a new deadline and that was on March 26th.

12193
13:29:52,870 --> 13:29:57,150
He gave Iran 10 days or until the evening of April 6th

12194
13:29:57,150 --> 13:29:59,430
to reopen the Strait.

12195
13:29:59,430 --> 13:30:02,550
Trump also issued his latest Hormuz threat on Sunday.

12196
13:30:02,550 --> 13:30:05,910
That's after vowing to bomb power plants and bridges

12197
13:30:05,910 --> 13:30:07,590
if Tehran doesn't comply.

12198
13:30:07,630 --> 13:30:11,430
He posted what appears to be a Tuesday 8 p.m. EST

12199
13:30:11,430 --> 13:30:14,230
eastern time that is deadline for a deal.

12200
13:30:14,230 --> 13:30:15,550
Well, Al Jazeera's Mike Hanna

12201
13:30:15,550 --> 13:30:19,700
has more on Trump's comments from Washington, D.C.

12202
13:30:19,700 --> 13:30:23,460
The unusual use of an expletive by a national leader,

12203
13:30:23,460 --> 13:30:27,180
perhaps a symbol of President Trump's frustration

12204
13:30:27,180 --> 13:30:28,860
with the Iranian government

12205
13:30:28,860 --> 13:30:31,540
and their refusal to concede to the demands

12206
13:30:31,540 --> 13:30:32,660
that he is making.

12207
13:30:32,660 --> 13:30:35,580
That reference as well was to the Strait of Hormuz

12208
13:30:35,580 --> 13:30:38,220
which in recent days, President Trump had insisted

12209
13:30:38,220 --> 13:30:39,860
he did not care about saying

12210
13:30:39,860 --> 13:30:42,900
the U.S. did not need the oil passing through the Strait

12211
13:30:42,900 --> 13:30:45,980
and it was up to the countries who are reliant on that oil

12212
13:30:45,980 --> 13:30:47,300
to deal with the situation.

12213
13:30:47,300 --> 13:30:50,540
But now the demand about opening the Strait of Hormuz

12214
13:30:50,540 --> 13:30:52,300
appears front and center

12215
13:30:52,300 --> 13:30:56,660
of the President's new demands of the Iranian government.

12216
13:30:56,660 --> 13:31:00,060
President Trump threatening to, and I use his words,

12217
13:31:00,060 --> 13:31:03,340
blowing everything and taking the oil

12218
13:31:03,380 --> 13:31:06,300
if Iran does not meet his new deadline,

12219
13:31:06,300 --> 13:31:08,380
which has now been set at 8 p.m.

12220
13:31:08,380 --> 13:31:11,100
eastern time on Tuesday evening.

12221
13:31:11,100 --> 13:31:13,340
He says in an earlier media post

12222
13:31:13,340 --> 13:31:16,500
that a power plant day and bridge day

12223
13:31:16,500 --> 13:31:18,780
all wrapped up on Tuesday.

12224
13:31:18,780 --> 13:31:21,340
But on the other hand, in addition to these threats,

12225
13:31:21,340 --> 13:31:23,180
President Trump is sending signals

12226
13:31:23,180 --> 13:31:26,420
that there's some kind of negotiation process underway.

12227
13:31:26,420 --> 13:31:30,300
He's indicated that his close confidants, Jared Kushner

12228
13:31:30,300 --> 13:31:33,260
and Stephen Whitcoff are in consultation

12229
13:31:33,260 --> 13:31:34,980
with either the Iranian government

12230
13:31:34,980 --> 13:31:38,380
and identified figures or some form of intermediary.

12231
13:31:38,380 --> 13:31:40,980
And speaking to U.S. news outlets,

12232
13:31:40,980 --> 13:31:43,740
President Trump says that he is optimistic

12233
13:31:43,740 --> 13:31:46,300
that there can be an agreement very soon.

12234
13:31:46,300 --> 13:31:48,300
He says the agreement could come

12235
13:31:48,300 --> 13:31:52,820
within a matter of days rather than a matter of weeks.

12236
13:31:52,820 --> 13:31:54,820
So you've got this dichotomous approach

12237
13:31:54,820 --> 13:31:57,620
from the President on the one hand threatening

12238
13:31:57,620 --> 13:32:01,500
obliteration to civilian targets within Iran,

12239
13:32:01,500 --> 13:32:04,940
which some observers would contend to be a war crime.

12240
13:32:04,940 --> 13:32:07,300
But on the other hand, what he is saying is,

12241
13:32:07,300 --> 13:32:10,220
yes, we are talking, the talks are going well,

12242
13:32:10,220 --> 13:32:12,340
and they could come to fruition

12243
13:32:12,340 --> 13:32:14,380
before that new deadline I set,

12244
13:32:14,380 --> 13:32:17,740
which is 8 p.m. eastern time on Tuesday.

12245
13:32:17,740 --> 13:32:20,940
Mike Hanna, Al Jazeera, Washington.

12246
13:32:20,940 --> 13:32:22,500
The Iran war is piling pressure

12247
13:32:22,500 --> 13:32:24,340
on Sri Lanka's fragile economy,

12248
13:32:24,340 --> 13:32:27,540
still recovering from its financial crisis four years ago.

12249
13:32:27,540 --> 13:32:28,980
Fuel prices have surged,

12250
13:32:28,980 --> 13:32:31,460
with petrol and diesel now being rationed.

12251
13:32:31,460 --> 13:32:34,460
Electricity costs are also up by 25%.

12252
13:32:34,460 --> 13:32:37,660
And that says Manel Fernandez reports for us from Colombo.

12253
13:32:37,660 --> 13:32:41,630
Many people are struggling to cope.

12254
13:32:41,630 --> 13:32:42,870
Lassit Gayan has worked

12255
13:32:42,870 --> 13:32:46,190
for a food delivery company in Colombo for four years.

12256
13:32:46,190 --> 13:32:48,070
The 39-year-old's income depends

12257
13:32:48,070 --> 13:32:50,430
on the number of deliveries he makes.

12258
13:32:50,430 --> 13:32:52,870
But restrictions on fuel and price increases

12259
13:32:52,870 --> 13:32:56,070
caused by the Iran war have affected his earnings.

12260
13:32:56,070 --> 13:32:59,190
I make around $20 a day,

12261
13:32:59,190 --> 13:33:00,670
but I have to buy all my meals.

12262
13:33:00,670 --> 13:33:02,510
That costs more than $5 a day.

12263
13:33:02,510 --> 13:33:04,230
I use what's left for fuel, rent,

12264
13:33:04,230 --> 13:33:06,480
and to send home to my family.

12265
13:33:06,480 --> 13:33:08,000
Restaurants like this,

12266
13:33:08,000 --> 13:33:10,720
where Gayan is picking up his first order for the day,

12267
13:33:10,720 --> 13:33:12,200
are also struggling.

12268
13:33:12,200 --> 13:33:15,080
Gas for cooking is more expensive.

12269
13:33:15,080 --> 13:33:17,480
And manager Suranga Tirunagama says

12270
13:33:17,480 --> 13:33:21,250
good quality ingredients are difficult to find.

12271
13:33:21,250 --> 13:33:24,650
This has forced many outlets to increase their prices.

12272
13:33:24,650 --> 13:33:28,130
Something Tirunagama says he's trying to avoid.

12273
13:33:28,130 --> 13:33:29,330
Can I have a pulon tiran price?

12274
13:33:29,330 --> 13:33:31,970
We're trying our best to manage without raising prices,

12275
13:33:31,970 --> 13:33:34,250
but it's getting more challenging day by day

12276
13:33:34,250 --> 13:33:36,610
because today's prices are not the same tomorrow.

12277
13:33:36,610 --> 13:33:37,770
We can't budget.

12278
13:33:37,770 --> 13:33:40,020
Prices are increasing.

12279
13:33:40,020 --> 13:33:41,780
And it's already evident.

12280
13:33:41,780 --> 13:33:45,260
Gayan says he's delivering few orders these days.

12281
13:33:45,260 --> 13:33:47,260
Many people we spoke to told us

12282
13:33:47,260 --> 13:33:50,020
the worst part is the uncertainty.

12283
13:33:50,020 --> 13:33:53,020
On the way to his next pickup, Gayan fills up.

12284
13:33:53,020 --> 13:33:55,820
The government has imposed fuel restrictions.

12285
13:33:55,820 --> 13:33:59,540
Motorbike riders get a weekly quarter of eight liters.

12286
13:33:59,540 --> 13:34:02,700
Half the fuel Gayan says he usually goes through.

12287
13:34:02,700 --> 13:34:06,900
Station owner Sampat Kotalavala is also dealing with uncertainty.

12288
13:34:06,900 --> 13:34:12,420
We only receive about 50% of the supplies we order.

12289
13:34:12,420 --> 13:34:14,700
And we manage these stocks according to the framework

12290
13:34:14,700 --> 13:34:15,940
the government has given us.

12291
13:34:15,940 --> 13:34:19,060
It's not enough for some, but generally it's okay.

12292
13:34:19,060 --> 13:34:20,020
But that's for today.

12293
13:34:20,020 --> 13:34:23,120
I can't say what tomorrow will be like.

12294
13:34:23,120 --> 13:34:25,280
There are other pressures too.

12295
13:34:25,280 --> 13:34:27,360
A long-pending electricity price increase

12296
13:34:27,360 --> 13:34:28,960
took effect this month,

12297
13:34:28,960 --> 13:34:32,780
with some bills set to go up by 25%.

12298
13:34:32,780 --> 13:34:36,420
The government has asked people to use power sparingly.

12299
13:34:36,420 --> 13:34:39,300
Ioning and washing clothes only once a week.

12300
13:34:39,300 --> 13:34:40,740
And government officers

12301
13:34:40,740 --> 13:34:43,900
have been told to switch off air conditioners early.

12302
13:34:43,900 --> 13:34:45,540
Gayan says Sri Lanka is recovering

12303
13:34:45,540 --> 13:34:47,700
from its worst economic crisis.

12304
13:34:47,700 --> 13:34:50,500
The Iran war is causing more uncertainty.

12305
13:34:50,500 --> 13:34:53,060
People are paying more for fuel, food

12306
13:34:53,060 --> 13:34:54,940
and even public transport

12307
13:34:54,940 --> 13:34:57,700
as a conflict thousands of kilometers away

12308
13:34:57,740 --> 13:34:59,700
since prices soaring.

12309
13:34:59,700 --> 13:35:03,460
On the road, Gayan has stopped for a cup of tea and a snack

12310
13:35:03,460 --> 13:35:07,140
that's costing him more now than it did two weeks ago.

12311
13:35:07,140 --> 13:35:10,740
But he must hurry because the next order is waiting.

12312
13:35:10,740 --> 13:35:14,340
Minal Fernandez, Al Jazeera, Colombo.

12313
13:35:14,340 --> 13:35:16,780
All right, let's take a look at some of the other world's news.

12314
13:35:16,780 --> 13:35:18,820
Israeli forces have shot and killed

12315
13:35:18,820 --> 13:35:21,540
a UN employee in Gaza and injured another.

12316
13:35:21,540 --> 13:35:23,700
The World Health Organization's staff members

12317
13:35:23,700 --> 13:35:26,300
were travelling in a vehicle along Salahid Dean Road

12318
13:35:26,300 --> 13:35:27,700
in southern Gaza.

12319
13:35:27,700 --> 13:35:30,300
And that's when Israeli soldiers opened fire.

12320
13:35:30,300 --> 13:35:33,750
Three other people were also injured in the attack.

12321
13:35:33,750 --> 13:35:36,750
Hamas says it will not hand over its weapons.

12322
13:35:36,750 --> 13:35:38,830
Disarmament is part of the second phase

12323
13:35:38,830 --> 13:35:40,510
of the Gaza ceasefire plan.

12324
13:35:40,510 --> 13:35:42,590
But the armed group says calls to lay down

12325
13:35:42,590 --> 13:35:44,470
its weapons are unacceptable,

12326
13:35:44,470 --> 13:35:46,510
especially as Palestinians continue

12327
13:35:46,510 --> 13:35:48,590
to be targeted by Israel.

12328
13:35:48,590 --> 13:35:50,590
More than 700 people have been killed

12329
13:35:50,590 --> 13:35:54,240
since the ceasefire came into effect in October.

12330
13:35:54,240 --> 13:35:58,320
As for raising the issue of weapons

12331
13:35:58,320 --> 13:36:01,560
in this crude manner, it is nothing but a scandalous attempt

12332
13:36:01,560 --> 13:36:03,640
by the occupation to continue killing

12333
13:36:03,640 --> 13:36:05,720
and genocide against our people,

12334
13:36:05,720 --> 13:36:09,040
which we will not accept under any circumstances.

12335
13:36:09,040 --> 13:36:11,880
We affirm that what the enemy was unable to seize from us

12336
13:36:11,880 --> 13:36:14,120
with tanks and genocide, it will not

12337
13:36:14,120 --> 13:36:18,120
seize from us with politics or at the negotiation table.

12338
13:36:18,120 --> 13:36:20,280
The occupation's aggression against our people

12339
13:36:20,280 --> 13:36:23,040
